1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,400
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۞ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۞

2
00:00:04,081 --> 00:00:08,685
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسليمًا كثيرا

3
00:00:10,237 --> 00:00:14,153
We talked about the battles of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Al-Ghazawaat(ألغزوات).

4
00:00:14,271 --> 00:00:15,837
Now we'll talk about the Sarayah(سراية)

5
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:20,153
and the greatest Sariyah(سرية) at all is called Ghazawa Mu'tah(غزوة مَؤتَة).

6
00:00:20,222 --> 00:00:23,114
So, it's given the title of Ghazwa(غزوة), Ghazawa Mu'tah(غزوة مَؤتَة) I mean.

7
00:00:23,957 --> 00:00:29,137
Ibn Nihass(ابن نحاس) says, it occurred in Jamada Al- Ula(جمادی الاولی) the eight of Hijrah(هجرة).

8
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:32,727
It was an army of 3000 headed by Zaid Ibn Harisa(زید ابن حارثه),

9
00:00:33,262 --> 00:00:35,210
they headed for Al-Balkaa(ألبلقاء) in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

10
00:00:35,601 --> 00:00:39,913
The Messenger of Allah gave his instructions to the army.

11
00:00:40,058 --> 00:00:43,078
If Zaid(زيد) is killed then Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفرابن ابی طالب) takes charge.

12
00:00:43,558 --> 00:00:46,102
And if he is killed, then Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبداللہ بن رواحة) leads.

13
00:00:46,397 --> 00:00:49,789
When they reached Ma'an(معان) in present day Jordan, they heard

14
00:00:50,014 --> 00:00:53,926
that the Roman Emperor has mobilized an army of 100,000 Roman soldiers,

15
00:00:54,295 --> 00:00:57,603
in addition to another 100,000 Arab tribesmen.

16
00:00:58,191 --> 00:01:01,091
Due to the sheer numbers of the enemies, some Muslims suggested

17
00:01:01,346 --> 00:01:04,846
writing to the Messenger of Allah to maybe send them reinforcements,

18
00:01:05,205 --> 00:01:06,705
or give them a different order.

19
00:01:07,892 --> 00:01:10,092
But Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) said: Oh, people,

20
00:01:10,366 --> 00:01:15,738
what you are fearing is what you came for in the first place, martyrdom.

21
00:01:16,236 --> 00:01:19,436
We do not fight our enemy with our numbers or our equipment,

22
00:01:19,577 --> 00:01:22,965
but we fight them with this religion, which Allah honored us with.

23
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:26,560
So let's fight! Both our options are great.

24
00:01:26,903 --> 00:01:29,075
 It is either going to be victory or martyrdom.

25
00:01:30,028 --> 00:01:32,428
This encouraged the Muslims and they decided to go ahead

26
00:01:32,527 --> 00:01:35,760
- and meet the army, 3000 faced 200,000.

27
00:01:35,941 --> 00:01:37,041
  Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) said:

28
00:01:38,409 --> 00:01:43,609
When the enemy's army approached, we saw what none of us could imagine in numbers and arms

29
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,440
my eyes quivered.

30
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:49,840
They never saw an army like this in their life.

31
00:01:50,718 --> 00:01:55,818
 So Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) said: My eyes just quivered when I saw, what I saw in front of me.

32
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,060
Sabit Ibn Arqam(ثابت إبن أرقم) told me:

33
00:01:58,194 --> 00:02:02,446
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) it seems that you are staring at a huge army.

34
00:02:03,221 --> 00:02:06,821
I said: Yes! He said: You were not with us at Badr(بدر)

35
00:02:07,227 --> 00:02:09,494
 we did not win due to our numbers.

36
00:02:10,477 --> 00:02:11,405
He is giving him to Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) a lessons,

37
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:15,752
see Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) became a Muslim, around the time of Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

38
00:02:16,584 --> 00:02:19,224
so he did not witness badr(بدر), Uhud(أحَد), Al-Khandaq(خندق).

39
00:02:20,215 --> 00:02:25,215
So Sabit(ثابت) is telling him that in Badr(بدر) we were very small army, 314.

40
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,103
Nevertheless, we went against our enemy.

41
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:32,526
A violent battle erupted the head of the Muslim armies Zaid(زيد) was killed.

42
00:02:32,728 --> 00:02:35,128
The leader of following him was Jafar(جعفر).

43
00:02:35,646 --> 00:02:37,846
His right hand carrying the banner was cut off,

44
00:02:37,969 --> 00:02:41,201
so he carried it with his left hand, which was then cut off.

45
00:02:42,178 --> 00:02:46,978
He then hugged it with what was left of both arms, until he was killed.

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,400
The third leader Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) took charge

47
00:02:50,956 --> 00:02:55,256
a cousin of his, gave him a piece of dried meat to eat, and told him,

48
00:02:55,534 --> 00:02:57,434
Strengthen yourself with this.

49
00:02:58,203 --> 00:03:02,003
You have went through a lot this day, he grabbed it and he took a bite.

50
00:03:02,635 --> 00:03:05,535
Then he told himself, you are still in this world.

51
00:03:06,268 --> 00:03:09,584
And he threw the piece of meat away and fought, until he was killed.

52
00:03:10,441 --> 00:03:13,841
The three successive leaders appointed by the Messenger of Allah fell dead.

53
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:18,710
So Zaid Bin Arqam(زید ابن ارقم) held the banner and told the Muslims to agree on a leader.

54
00:03:19,178 --> 00:03:20,578
They said: You! He said: No!

55
00:03:20,764 --> 00:03:21,764
Find someone else.

56
00:03:22,341 --> 00:03:23,641
They chose Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

57
00:03:24,238 --> 00:03:28,438
He fought for a while and then planned the retreat and decided to go back to Madina.

58
00:03:28,656 --> 00:03:30,456
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was a new Muslim then.

59
00:03:31,542 --> 00:03:35,542
While the battle was still running hundreds of miles away, the Messenger of Allah said:

60
00:03:36,183 --> 00:03:38,183
Zaid(زيد) held the banner and was killed.

61
00:03:38,413 --> 00:03:41,273
Then the banner was carried by Jafar(جعفر), who was also killed.

62
00:03:41,817 --> 00:03:45,317
And then, it was carried by Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة), who was also killed.

63
00:03:45,856 --> 00:03:51,056
Then the banner was carried by a sword from Allah and opening would occur on his hands.

64
00:03:51,551 --> 00:03:55,851
And that's when Rasool Allah ﷺ gave Khalid(خالد) the title, of Sword of Allah.

65
00:03:56,717 --> 00:04:01,117
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) poses the question, Was Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) defeat or victory?

66
00:04:01,529 --> 00:04:03,929
He says: Some considered it to be a defeat.

67
00:04:05,102 --> 00:04:08,702
Some consider it to be neither defeat nor victory.

68
00:04:09,754 --> 00:04:13,254
While many scholars considered Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) to be a victory for the Muslims,

69
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:17,230
among these are Al-Waqdi(ألواقعدي), Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر).

70
00:04:18,145 --> 00:04:21,145
Al-Waqdi(ألواقعدي) says: When Khalid(خالد) became the leader,

71
00:04:21,856 --> 00:04:26,436
he fought for the rest of the day and then during their rest at night,

72
00:04:26,734 --> 00:04:28,834
- he had the Muslim army reconfigure.

73
00:04:29,151 --> 00:04:32,855
 So he had the left flank move to the right, and vice versa.

74
00:04:34,031 --> 00:04:39,279
So the next day when the Romans saw the change, they thought that the Muslims had received reinforcements.

75
00:04:39,868 --> 00:04:43,364
What Khalid(خالد) did, all what he did was, he switched the flanks.

76
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:47,508
So the Romans wake up in the next day in the morning, they find new faces in front of them.

77
00:04:47,866 --> 00:04:49,742
They said: Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) we have a new army.

78
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:55,360
 So they retreated, and when they retreated, Khalid(خالد) also retreated.

79
00:04:56,273 --> 00:05:02,945
In Bukhari(بخاريْ) Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) says: During the Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) nine swords broke in my hand,

80
00:05:03,371 --> 00:05:06,863
only a Yemeni firm sword I had survived on that day.

81
00:05:07,014 --> 00:05:12,946
Imagine breaking nine swords, these are solid pieces of steel

82
00:05:13,554 --> 00:05:14,454
- they were breaking.

83
00:05:15,072 --> 00:05:18,805
In Topkapi museum in Istanbul

84
00:05:20,032 --> 00:05:22,832
They have a lot of the relics of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

85
00:05:23,516 --> 00:05:25,816
and they have a sword that they claim,

86
00:05:26,646 --> 00:05:27,995
- belongs to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

87
00:05:28,019 --> 00:05:31,519
Now Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم)  how valid of these claims are,

88
00:05:31,548 --> 00:05:34,948
because they have a tooth, they said: It belong to Rasool Ullah, a hair, it belongs to Rasool Ullah,

89
00:05:35,545 --> 00:05:37,745
they had a few different swords of Al-Abbas(العباس),

90
00:05:37,810 --> 00:05:39,561
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

91
00:05:41,003 --> 00:05:45,679
but anyway, I remember one of those swords, I think it belonged to Al-Abbas(العباس),

92
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:51,946
 It was this huge piece of quill Yani(يعني) very long and thick.

93
00:05:52,753 --> 00:05:57,353
I mean, just carrying it with would be an effort in itself,

94
00:05:57,594 --> 00:06:00,494
let alone fighting with it for an entire day.

95
00:06:01,346 --> 00:06:05,510
They must have had some serious physical strength,

96
00:06:06,106 --> 00:06:10,006
to be able to fight with such a sword for a whole day.

97
00:06:10,853 --> 00:06:18,677
Tayeb(طيِّب) other armies, the Messenger of Allah sent, headed by his companions and I'll just go through these.

98
00:06:20,294 --> 00:06:25,438
These are Sarayah(سراية) to show you how active the military scene was,

99
00:06:25,728 --> 00:06:31,328
 you know when that guy said that when Rasool Allah ﷺ only fought for 19 days in Madina,

100
