339
00:25:40,282 --> 00:25:42,639
In fact, the Masjid Al-Amvi(مسجدألأموي) was a church.

340
00:25:42,758 --> 00:25:44,433
It was the main Cathedral of the town.

341
00:25:44,948 --> 00:25:49,900
It was split in half, half of it Masjid(مسجد) and half of it church

342
00:25:49,956 --> 00:25:53,395
and eventually Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة) they bought the whole thing and it became a Masjid Al-Amvi(مسجدألأموي),

343
00:25:53,657 --> 00:25:55,689
but they, they bought it they paid for it.

344
00:25:57,426 --> 00:25:59,857
In 15 Hijri(هجري), the great battle of Yarmook(يرموك) occurred.

345
00:25:59,937 --> 00:26:06,321
The Muslims were 30,000 headed by Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة), while the Romans were 300,000 strong.

346
00:26:06,431 --> 00:26:08,715
Yani(يعني) he says here it is headed by Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة),

347
00:26:08,755 --> 00:26:12,317
while At-Tabri(ألطبري) considers that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was the leader in Yarmook(يرموك).

348
00:26:13,455 --> 00:26:16,066
Even though they were 10 times the size of the Muslim army.

349
00:26:16,476 --> 00:26:22,084
Their soldiers had to be tied together in chains to ensure they do not flee the battlefield.

350
00:26:23,008 --> 00:26:26,847
However, these same chain turned out To be a disaster for them,

351
00:26:27,272 --> 00:26:31,641
since when they were defeated if one of the soldiers would try to run for his life,

352
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:34,490
he would drag down everyone else with him.

353
00:26:34,903 --> 00:26:40,956
And they were on the edge of a canyon 10s of 1000s of them ended up falling from that Canyon.

354
00:26:41,973 --> 00:26:46,620
The raider of the battle, who would go around inspiring the Muslims was Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

355
00:26:47,144 --> 00:26:51,036
He would call out loud: O victory of Allah come to us.

356
00:26:52,483 --> 00:26:57,061
In 15 Hijri(هجري) also, that's when the great battle of Al-Qadsia(ألقادسية) occurred.

357
00:26:57,918 --> 00:27:03,468
The Muslims were 8000 headed by Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص), the Persians were 60,000 headed by Rustum(رُسْتُم).

358
00:27:04,150 --> 00:27:06,180
It was a crushing defeat for the Persians,

359
00:27:06,587 --> 00:27:10,214
Rustum(رُسْتُم), along with 1000s of his soldiers were killed.

360
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:13,291
Al-Qadsia(ألقادسية) was the key that opened the rest of Persia.

361
00:27:13,996 --> 00:27:16,834
In 16, the Battle of Jalulaa(جلولاء) occurred.

362
00:27:17,199 --> 00:27:23,173
In this battle, almost 100,000 persians were killed, and they left behind the great booty.

363
00:27:23,413 --> 00:27:28,796
Within three years the Muslims have opened the seat of the Persian empires throne

364
00:27:29,145 --> 00:27:31,651
and have taken the jewels of the Roman Empire.

365
00:27:31,970 --> 00:27:34,676
So Glory be to Allah the Great and the Exalted.

366
00:27:35,638 --> 00:27:41,503
In year 16 Hijri(هجري), Umar(عُمَر) himself traveled to Jerusalem to accept the keys to the city

367
00:27:42,241 --> 00:27:47,410
and there's a famous story of the journey of Umar(عُمَر) to Jerusalem(یروشلم).

368
00:27:48,307 --> 00:27:57,276
See the Roman patriarchs, the religious authority of Jerusalem, which was a Christian town at the time.

369
00:27:58,117 --> 00:28:04,507
They knew that it's inevitable that they will have to give up the city of Jerusalem.

370
00:28:05,237 --> 00:28:11,222
But they saw that it's not appropriate for this Great blessed city to be delivered

371
00:28:11,753 --> 00:28:17,098
to a secondary leader among the Muslims, but it should be given to the Khalifah(خليفه) himself.

372
00:28:17,690 --> 00:28:29,775
The status of Jerusalem demands that the keys of it needs to be transferred to the main man, Khalifah(خليفه) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

373
00:28:31,450 --> 00:28:35,885
So they told Umar(عُمَر) to come and receive the keys to the holy city.

374
00:28:36,258 --> 00:28:40,058
So Umar(عُمَر) traveled with his servant, just the two of them.

375
00:28:41,059 --> 00:28:47,688
They had one camel they would take turns.

376
00:28:49,531 --> 00:28:51,701
1/3 of the time Umar(عُمَر) is riding the camel,

377
00:28:51,971 --> 00:28:54,376
1/3 of the time his servant is riding the camel,

378
00:28:54,653 --> 00:28:59,614
and 1/3 of the time they're both walking in the camel is taking rest.

379
00:29:02,087 --> 00:29:07,763
It happened that when they were on the outskirts of the city of Jerusalem, it was the servants turn.

380
00:29:09,232 --> 00:29:11,483
So Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) sees this scene in front of his eyes.

381
00:29:11,563 --> 00:29:20,119
He's seeing Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the Khalifah(خليفه) holding on to the camel, and the servants is riding.

382
00:29:20,907 --> 00:29:24,177
And then he is wearing this thoub(ثوب) that has 14 patches in it.

383
00:29:24,645 --> 00:29:28,486
And then he comes across a pool of water and mud.

384
00:29:29,105 --> 00:29:32,691
And Umar(عُمَر) is lifting up as though and crossing through the mud.

385
00:29:33,674 --> 00:29:42,346
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) goes to Umar(عُمَر) and says that these Romans they have some formalities and they have some etiquettes,

386
00:29:42,878 --> 00:29:45,769
he's trying to tell the Khalifah(خليفه) that this is not the Madina

387
00:29:46,571 --> 00:29:52,869
and he's trying to give suggestions to the Khalifah(خليفه) and Khalifah(خليفه) is listening to the Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) is saying.

388
00:29:53,129 --> 00:29:54,683
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) has best of intention.

389
00:29:55,302 --> 00:30:00,342
Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) is doing that because he doesn't want the Romans to get the wrong impression.

390
00:30:01,151 --> 00:30:05,217
It's to keep and preserve the reputation of the Muslims that's the reason.

391
00:30:06,823 --> 00:30:11,185
It's not because of any inferiority complex we have to look like them or something.

392
00:30:11,225 --> 00:30:16,236
No, that's not it, but we have a certain reputation in their eyes and we want to keep it,

393
00:30:17,854 --> 00:30:21,050
we have that Izzah(عزة) and we want to retain that Izzah(عزة).

394
00:30:22,156 --> 00:30:24,556
So the issue with Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) is Izzah(عزة).

395
00:30:26,865 --> 00:30:33,811
And he didn't want the Khalifah(خليفه) to be seen in a position that compromises that image of Izzah(عزة).

396
00:30:35,128 --> 00:30:38,211
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is listening what Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) has to say.

397
00:30:38,612 --> 00:30:42,602
And then he hits his chest with his hand and says,

398
00:30:42,650 --> 00:30:44,329
ابوعبيدة لوقالها غيرك

399
00:30:44,976 --> 00:30:50,396
If somebody else would have said that, meaning I don't expect these words to come from somebody like you.

400
00:30:51,381 --> 00:30:55,963
You know, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) has so much respect and love for Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة).

401
00:30:56,754 --> 00:31:05,608
One day, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he was sitting with some of the Sahabah(صحابه), in a room, and he told them:

402
00:31:05,648 --> 00:31:06,270
تمنوا

403
00:31:06,835 --> 00:31:08,051
Make a wish.

404
00:31:09,345 --> 00:31:10,225
So one of them said:

405
00:31:10,265 --> 00:31:15,591
أتمنى لو أن لي هذه الدار مملوءة ذهبا أنفقه في سبيل الله

406
00:31:16,266 --> 00:31:21,468
I wish that Allah would fill this room with gold, so that I can spend it in the path of Allah.

407
00:31:21,948 --> 00:31:23,710
Umar(عُمَر) said: Tamanoo(تمنوا)! Make a wish.

408
00:31:24,062 --> 00:31:25,165
The other one said:

409
00:31:25,582 --> 00:31:32,392
I wish that this room would be filled with pearls and jewels, so I can spend them in the path of Allah.

410
00:31:32,853 --> 00:31:34,237
Umar(عُمَر) said: Tamanoo(تمنوا)! Make a wish.

411
00:31:34,317 --> 00:31:36,684
They said: What else can we say?

412
00:31:37,673 --> 00:31:39,345
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said.

413
00:31:39,837 --> 00:31:47,246
أمَّا أنَا فاتمنى لو أنِّي هذا الغرفة رجال مثل أبي عبيدة بن الجراح

414
00:31:47,690 --> 00:31:52,722
I wish if Allah will fill up this room with men like Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح).

415
00:31:53,785 --> 00:31:57,523
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not leave behind gold, he did not leave behind pearls.

416
00:31:57,857 --> 00:32:00,567
He did not leave behind wonderful Islamic architecture.

417
00:32:01,424 --> 00:32:08,606
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not write any books, but Rasool Allah ﷺ carved the Qur'an, into the hearts of 10,000 men.

418
00:32:09,074 --> 00:32:09,979
That's what he did!

419
00:32:10,503 --> 00:32:12,527
Rasool Allah ﷺ left behind men.

420
00:32:13,558 --> 00:32:20,470
Rasool Allah ﷺ, the harvest of his effort of 23 years was men.

421
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:25,436
In terms of the infrastructure in terms of the institutions in terms of all of that,

422
00:32:25,697 --> 00:32:30,316
none of it was done by Rasool Allah ﷺ, those were things that the Khulafah(خلفاء) later on did.

423
00:32:31,816 --> 00:32:40,461
Rasool Allah ﷺ his Masjid(مسجد), was built out of mud bricks, and it had the roof of palm leaves.

424
00:32:40,968 --> 00:32:47,293
And when it would rain, it would drip on their heads, and there was no carpet they used to pray on sand.

425
00:32:48,493 --> 00:32:51,577
However, it has every blessing that we have today.

426
00:32:51,982 --> 00:32:56,238
The palaces that are built in Al-Hamra(ألحمراء), and Damascus and Baghdad

427
00:32:56,995 --> 00:33:07,796
and the wealth that the Ummah(امة) had and has today is all a fruit of the effort of all Rasool Allah ﷺ those 10,000 men that he left behind.

428
00:33:08,550 --> 00:33:14,036
Every blessing and every Barakah(بركة), that we have, we're living off what Rasool Allah ﷺ left us.

429
00:33:15,155 --> 00:33:17,213
He left behind the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

430
00:33:17,933 --> 00:33:22,381
So, Umar(عُمَر) when he said that the Sahabah(صحابه) said:

431
00:33:22,461 --> 00:33:24,445
May Allah reward you for that advice.

432
00:33:25,532 --> 00:33:30,810
This was an advice, Yani(يعني) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the whole point of this story

433
00:33:31,326 --> 00:33:33,532
is to give them a Naseeha(نَصيحة), to give them an advice.

434
00:33:33,675 --> 00:33:36,942
That it is, this religion changes the heart of men.

435
00:33:38,659 --> 00:33:43,074
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said, if somebody else said that Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة).

436
00:33:44,034 --> 00:33:49,639
نحن قوم أعزَّنا الله بالإسلام فمهما ابتغينا العزَّة في غيره أذلَّنا الله

437
00:33:50,583 --> 00:33:56,298
We were people who were humiliated before Islam and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honored us through Islam.

438
00:33:56,853 --> 00:34:01,019
And if we seek honor in any other way, Allah will humiliate us again.

439
00:34:02,726 --> 00:34:08,440
Our honor did not come because of our clothes, or because of the transportation that we're using,

440
00:34:09,782 --> 00:34:11,821
or because of security guards and show.

441
00:34:12,615 --> 00:34:14,521
Our honor comes because of Islam.

442
00:34:15,831 --> 00:34:18,234
In year 20 the battle of Tastur(تستر) happened.

443
00:34:19,052 --> 00:34:22,752
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) had laid siege to the powerful city for over a year.

444
00:34:23,306 --> 00:34:26,956
The Persian general Al- Hurmuzan(ألهرمزان) was fortified in there.

445
00:34:27,472 --> 00:34:29,826
A Persian man came to Abu Musa(أبوموسى) and told him:

446
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:35,639
If you promise me and my family protection I will guide you to a secret entrance into the city.

447
00:34:37,242 --> 00:34:42,720
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) gave him protection, so he sent with him Majza'ah Bin Thawr(مجزعة بن ثور).

448
00:34:43,392 --> 00:34:50,039
They entered through a hidden underground spring of water, swimming through it until they surfaced in the city.

449
00:34:50,935 --> 00:34:56,102
They entered the city and Majza'ah(مجزعة) traveled through it, until he learned its map.

450
00:34:57,110 --> 00:35:01,114
So, Majza'ah(مجزعة) was swimming through this underground stream.

451
00:35:01,972 --> 00:35:07,823
He surfaces in the city walks around the city and he makes a mental map of the entire city.

452
00:35:13,613 --> 00:35:17,503
The Persian man also pointed out to him the Persian general Hurmuzan(ألهرمزان).

453
00:35:18,003 --> 00:35:22,915
Majza'ah(مجزعة) returned and was sent along with 35 men to conquer the city.

454
00:35:24,090 --> 00:35:29,864
The thirty-five men swam through the spring and entered the city at night and fought courageously.

455
00:35:30,324 --> 00:35:31,427
Majza'ah(مجزعة) was martyred.

456
00:35:32,173 --> 00:35:37,521
The fight continued and the Muslims ended up missing Fajr(فجر) and only prayed it at the middle of the day.

457
00:35:38,446 --> 00:35:40,228
The Persians surrendered.

458
00:35:40,533 --> 00:35:43,297
Al-Hurmuzan(ألهرمزان) became a Muslim and settled in Madina.

459
00:35:45,114 --> 00:35:48,964
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) opened Alexandria in year 21 by defeating the Romans.

460
00:35:49,376 --> 00:35:55,688
He then established a Muslim garrison in the city, while he descended south fighting the Muqawqas(مقوقس), the king of Egypt.

461
00:35:56,544 --> 00:36:05,176
But the Romans headed by Constantine the son of Hercules sent a naval army that entered Alexandria

462
00:36:05,510 --> 00:36:07,361
and killed the Muslim soldiers in it.

463
00:36:07,907 --> 00:36:09,710
Amr(عمرو) attacked and entered it again.

464
00:36:10,407 --> 00:36:13,610
In year 21 occurred the battle of Nahwand(نهوند) against the Persians.

465
00:36:13,951 --> 00:36:19,309
It was a furious battle, the Persians tied themselves in chains to prevent the escape of soldiers.

466
00:36:20,875 --> 00:36:23,113
The leader of the Muslim army was An-Numan Bin Maqran(ألنعمان بن مقرن).

467
00:36:23,677 --> 00:36:27,302
His horse fell down and he was then shot by an arrow and died.

468
00:36:27,722 --> 00:36:32,477
Hudaifa(حذيفة) took charge and the Muslims won after about 100,000 of the enemy were killed.

469
00:36:34,191 --> 00:36:38,470
In year 27 Muawiya Bin Abi Sufyan(معاويةبن أبي سفيان) opened the Island of Cyprus.

470
00:36:39,002 --> 00:36:43,851
Also during the same year Abdullah Bin Saad Bin Abi Sarh(عبدالله بن سعد بن أبي سرح) entered Africa.

471
00:36:44,835 --> 00:36:49,089
Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن زبير) killed the Roman leader of Africa Jarjeer(جرجير).

472
00:36:50,362 --> 00:36:57,115
In year 37 Abdullah Bin Hazm As-Sulami(عبدالله بن حزم ألسُلَمي) opened Herat(هرات) in Afghanistan, and Maru(مرو) in Turkistan.

473
00:36:57,893 --> 00:37:02,858
During the same year Al-Harith Bin Murrah Al Fehri(ألحارث بن مرَّة ألفِحري) entered Baluchistan.

474
00:37:04,414 --> 00:37:07,937
In year 44 Al-Muhalab Bin Abi Sufrah(ألمحلب بن أبي صفرى) entered India.

475
00:37:08,841 --> 00:37:14,657
In year 63 Uqbah Bin Nafie(عقبةبن نافع) fought in North Africa with the king of the Berbers, Kaseelah.

476
00:37:15,246 --> 00:37:20,988
Uqbah(عقبة) was martyred, his successor Zuhair Bin Qais Al-Balawi(زهير بن قيس ألبلوي) defeated them and killed the Berber king.

477
00:37:22,325 --> 00:37:27,483
In year 84 Musa Bin Nusair(موسى بن نصير) entered the land of Andalusia(أندلوسية), Spain.

478
00:37:28,156 --> 00:37:31,910
In year 87 the land of Bukhara(بخارة) was opened by Qutaybah Bin Muslim(قطيبة بن مسلم).

479
00:37:32,617 --> 00:37:37,735
In year 88 Maslamah Bin AbdulMalik(مسلمة بن عبدالملك) defeated the Romans in a number of battles.

480
00:37:38,473 --> 00:37:44,665
Qutaybah Bin Muslim(قطيبة بن مسلم) entered the land of the Turks and in year 90 he entered Taliqaan(طالقان).

481
00:37:46,054 --> 00:37:52,285
In year 93 Qutaybah(قطيبة) headed for Samarkand and opened it along with the surrounding areas.

482
00:37:52,721 --> 00:37:59,844
In year 95 Musa Bin Nusair(موسى بن نصير) completed his opening of the land of Andalusia and returned from it with an immense booty.

483
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:04,642
In year 98 Yazeed Bin Al Muhalab(يزيد بن ألمحلب) opened Taburstan(تبرستان).

484
00:38:05,295 --> 00:38:10,906
In the same year the Khalifah Sulayman Bin AbdulMalik(سليمان بن عبدالملك) sent a huge army to open Constantinople.

485
00:38:11,524 --> 00:38:16,067
The army was headed by his brother Maslamah(مسلمة), they besieged the city for 30 months.

486
00:38:16,468 --> 00:38:19,167
During that the Muslims suffered a lot of hardship.

487
00:38:19,647 --> 00:38:23,612
When Umar Bin AbdulAziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) became Khalifah(خليفه) he immediately recalled the army.

488
00:38:25,480 --> 00:38:32,683
During the era of the Abbasids fighting continued on the Eastern front towards India and China

489
00:38:33,034 --> 00:38:35,417
and the Northern front in the land of the Romans

490
00:38:35,716 --> 00:38:39,411
and the Western front towards Western Europe, Spain, France and Portugal.

491
00:38:40,337 --> 00:38:44,974
When the Crusaders attacked Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) the Muslims fought them in various battles.

492
00:38:45,468 --> 00:38:48,798
Among the Muslim leaders who fought them was Sultan Nur-Din Zinki(سلطان نورالدين زنكي)

493
00:38:49,231 --> 00:38:53,124
who retrieved a lot of the Muslim territory taken by the Crusaders.

494
00:38:53,420 --> 00:38:55,790
He was followed by Salahuddeen(صلاح الدين) who opened Jerusalem.

495
00:38:56,626 --> 00:39:02,655
When the Mongols flooded the Muslim land Jihad(جهاد) was fought against them in numerous battles.

496
00:39:02,974 --> 00:39:05,599
The Muslims won in the great battle of Ayn Jaloot(عين جالوت).

497
00:39:06,141 --> 00:39:12,337
The door of Jihad(جهاد) is always open and the fighting of the nonbelievers would never end until the Day of Judgment..

498
00:39:13,041 --> 00:39:16,677
So this is a brief chapter on the history of Jihad(جهاد).

499
00:39:23,921 --> 00:39:24,936
Chapter 15,

500
00:39:25,373 --> 00:39:26,357
COURAGE AND FEAR.

501
00:39:32,436 --> 00:39:37,046
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated: The strong believer is more beloved to Allah than the weak believer.

502
00:39:37,086 --> 00:39:38,150
And that's in Sahih Al-Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم).

503
00:39:39,031 --> 00:39:43,239
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to say: O Allah I seek refuge in you from gloom and Sorrow,

504
00:39:43,865 --> 00:39:49,334
from inaction and laziness, and from cowardice, stinginess and old age,

505
00:39:49,612 --> 00:39:52,762
and I seek refuge in you from the punishment of the grave.

506
00:39:53,739 --> 00:39:56,077
اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْهَمِّ وَالْحَزَنِ،

507
00:39:56,657 --> 00:39:58,244
 وأَعُوذُ بِكَ وَالْعَجْزِ وَالْكَسَلِ،

508
00:39:58,474 --> 00:39:59,928
وأَعُوذُ بِكَ وَالْبُخْلِ وَالْجُبْنِ ،

509
00:40:00,214 --> 00:40:02,100
وأَعُوذُ بِكَ وَضَلَعِ الدَّيْنِ، وَغَلَبَةِ الرِّجَالِ

510
00:40:02,180 --> 00:40:11,043
Very important Dua(دُعَا) to make because you are human and fear is a natural human thing.

511
00:40:13,069 --> 00:40:17,113
Everyone has fear, it's just a matter of degree.

512
00:40:17,613 --> 00:40:19,440
Some people have more fear than others.

513
00:40:20,406 --> 00:40:25,948
Your fear needs to be channeled to the right direction rather than fearing the creation, you fear Allah.

514
00:40:26,757 --> 00:40:34,185
Al-Izza Bin Abdul Salam(ألعزَّة بن عبدالسلام) when he went to visit a tyrant, one of Mangol.

515
00:40:35,848 --> 00:40:37,983
He was company by his students.

516
00:40:39,419 --> 00:40:41,367
So he started giving him Naseeha(نَصيحة),

517
00:40:42,780 --> 00:40:49,096
and he was becoming louder and louder and suddenly he was pointing fingers towards this tyrant.

518
00:40:50,041 --> 00:40:54,038
So the students were very, very afraid, worried.

519
00:40:55,482 --> 00:40:56,871
He could just chop off your head.

520
00:40:57,340 --> 00:41:08,219
So when they came out they said: How did you dare to speak to the tyrant in such confidence and strong way.

521
00:41:08,282 --> 00:41:08,872
He said:

522
00:41:10,288 --> 00:41:19,516
When I saw him and then I imagined the greatness of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, he became smaller in my eyes than a cat.

523
00:41:20,739 --> 00:41:22,177
I saw him smaller than a cat.

524
00:41:22,756 --> 00:41:26,335
But that's only when I started thinking about the Azamah(عظمى) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

525
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:34,786
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) was accompanying a delegation from Damascus to go and meet the head of a ta’tarr(تتار)

526
00:41:36,211 --> 00:41:46,772
and ta’tar(تتار) were like a swarm of locusts that was destroying everything that comes in its path.

527
00:41:49,479 --> 00:41:53,400
So they wanted to go and visit this king and to try to convince him.

528
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:56,069
And by the way at the time that the tat’arr(تتار) were already Muslim,

529
00:41:56,942 --> 00:41:59,576
See, they became Muslim but they carried on with their tyranny.

530
00:41:59,616 --> 00:42:04,039
It took them some time, time for Islam to sink in and for them to get it.

531
00:42:05,452 --> 00:42:12,714
This, this ta’tarr(تتار) king, he actually had the mobile Mimber(ممبر) and Mehrab(محراب) with him,

532
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:18,499
that he would carry along and then hired Imam(اِمَام) to lead Salah(صلاة) and to make Adhan(آذَان).

533
00:42:19,067 --> 00:42:25,567
So, Yani(يعني) once Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) was walking with his students and they saw them drinking.

534
00:42:26,368 --> 00:42:28,367
They saw these Mangol drinking.

535
00:42:28,789 --> 00:42:29,895
So the students they wanted to make,

536
00:42:29,935 --> 00:42:31,304
أمربالمعروف ونهي عن المنكر

537
00:42:31,824 --> 00:42:32,747
They wanted to stop them.

538
00:42:33,062 --> 00:42:34,661
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) said: Let them drink.

539
00:42:35,082 --> 00:42:39,288
Let them carry on, if they're sober, they're going to be killing Muslims,

540
00:42:39,629 --> 00:42:42,655
if they're drunk, they would leave the Muslims alone.

541
00:42:43,297 --> 00:42:44,647
So let them carry on and drink.

542
00:42:44,948 --> 00:42:53,496
So they went and in this delegation and you know in delegations you supposed to follow the etiquettes there's another protocol.

543
00:42:53,718 --> 00:42:58,643
You need to follow the protocol of how to speak and how to act and what should be said.

544
00:42:59,945 --> 00:43:06,224
So they go in there and obviously the Shaikh(شيخ) among them is Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) and everybody had something to say.

545
00:43:06,843 --> 00:43:12,089
So now this king said, requested Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) to make a Dua(دُعَا).

546
00:43:12,819 --> 00:43:14,041
Make a Dua(دُعَا) for us O Shaikh(شيخ).

547
00:43:15,022 --> 00:43:16,936
So Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) started making a Dua(دُعَا).

548
00:43:17,603 --> 00:43:24,429
And then he started making Dua(دُعَا) against the king and the king is saying Ameen(آمين), Ameen(آمين).

549
00:43:26,738 --> 00:43:31,801
Everyone in the delegation their knees started cracking shaking, trembling.

550
00:43:33,852 --> 00:43:40,640
It is said that they started wrapping up the clothes because they expected the sword to chop off his head at any moment.

551
00:43:41,451 --> 00:43:43,490
And they didn't want the blood to splash all over them.

552
00:43:44,109 --> 00:43:47,549
But it was a Hifz(حفظ) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ  that this king has no clue what Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) is saying:

553
00:43:47,589 --> 00:43:48,433
He's just saying, Ameen(آمين).

554
00:43:49,517 --> 00:43:55,223
As soon as they left the quarters of the king.

555
00:43:56,132 --> 00:43:59,835
The delegation came to Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) and said: Are you crazy, what have you done!

556
00:44:01,576 --> 00:44:05,070
And they started blaming him and yelling at them and then they said:

557
00:44:05,862 --> 00:44:09,688
Listen, we never want you to accompany us again.

558
00:44:10,254 --> 00:44:14,327
You go your way, we're gonna go ours, he said fine, you go your way, I'm gonna go mine.

559
00:44:15,209 --> 00:44:21,229
He and his students, alone, went one way and the entire delegation went another way.

560
00:44:23,436 --> 00:44:28,169
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) gets into Damascus and is waiting for this delegation to arrive what happens is they got raided.

561
00:44:28,729 --> 00:44:33,029
They got raided by some armed burglars who stole everything they have,

562
00:44:35,069 --> 00:44:37,790
and Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) reaches the town safely and securely.

563
00:44:37,965 --> 00:44:39,399
It is the Hifz(حفظ) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

564
00:44:40,439 --> 00:44:45,392
They have feared the creation, and they have not feared Allah.

565
00:44:45,472 --> 00:44:48,274
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ put them through this punishment,

566
00:44:48,635 --> 00:44:51,749
while Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) because he feared Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, Allah protected him.

567
00:44:55,264 --> 00:45:00,890
Notice that Rasool Allah ﷺ combined between seeking refuge in Allah from gloom and sorrow.

568
00:45:01,525 --> 00:45:02,518
الْهَمِّ وَالْحَزَنِ

569
00:45:03,082 --> 00:45:09,632
For gloom is the fear of what is coming, while sorrow is sadness on what has already passed.

570
00:45:11,452 --> 00:45:14,767
Al-Hum(هَمِّ) is concerned for something that is coming.

571
00:45:15,246 --> 00:45:20,921
Actually the whole reason why we learn this Dua(دُعَا) is because Rasool Allah ﷺ came into the Masjid(مسجد).

572
00:45:21,628 --> 00:45:26,753
And he saw one of the Sahabah(صحابه) laying on his back in the Masjid(مسجد) during business hours.

573
00:45:27,587 --> 00:45:29,825
So Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Don't you have any work to do.?

574
00:45:30,301 --> 00:45:30,604
He said:

575
00:45:30,644 --> 00:45:32,211
يا رسول الله ديونٌ

576
00:45:32,769 --> 00:45:35,142
O Messenger of Allah, I'm in debt.

577
00:45:35,777 --> 00:45:40,380
I have concerns about all of the debts that I have accumulated,

578
00:45:40,840 --> 00:45:42,658
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Say this Dua(دُعَا),

579
00:45:43,039 --> 00:45:44,945
اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْهَمِّ وَالْحَزَنِ

580
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:49,582
So this man was fearing for the future, how is he gonna pay all of these debts?

581
00:45:51,494 --> 00:45:56,009
So the Muslim should not feel sorry for the past nor fear the future.

582
00:45:57,400 --> 00:45:59,990
And he combined between inaction and laziness

583
00:46:00,361 --> 00:46:05,834
for inaction is the state of the heart, while laziness is the state of the body.

584
00:46:06,031 --> 00:46:07,676
وَالْعَجْزِ وَالْكَسَلِ

585
00:46:08,659 --> 00:46:12,719
Ajaz(عجز) is in heart and Kasal(كسل) is in the body.

586
00:46:13,997 --> 00:46:17,197
He combined between stinginess and cowardice,

587
00:46:17,473 --> 00:46:18,897
 وَالْجُبْنِ وَالْبُخْلِ

588
00:46:19,338 --> 00:46:22,815
For stinginess is the unwillingness to give wealth for Allah,

589
00:46:23,145 --> 00:46:26,326
while cowardice is the unwillingness to give the soul for Allah.

590
00:46:29,247 --> 00:46:30,438
How to overcome fear?

591
00:46:33,374 --> 00:46:35,698
Cowardice is the opposite of courage.

592
00:46:36,589 --> 00:46:38,804
And courage is the firmness of the heart.

593
00:46:39,415 --> 00:46:42,232
The heart is the essence of every good deed.

594
00:46:42,804 --> 00:46:45,870
The heart cannot be firm if the mind isn’t sound.

595
00:46:46,589 --> 00:46:53,649
If the heart is weak it leads to cowardice, and if the heart is too strong it leads to recklessness.

596
00:46:54,619 --> 00:46:58,871
The coward needs to cure cowardice by eliminating its cause.

597
00:46:59,368 --> 00:47:03,068
If it is caused by ignorance then ignorance is cured by learning.

598
00:47:03,876 --> 00:47:09,815
The cause could be fear of the unknown and that is cured by experiencing situations.

599
00:47:10,628 --> 00:47:18,604
We find that the beginner in public speaking experiences fear in the beginning but after experience this fear is overcome.

600
00:47:19,398 --> 00:47:24,599
We find that when a person first meets a king they might fear the occasion

601
00:47:24,884 --> 00:47:28,607
and their tongue would be tied and their posture would change.

602
00:47:29,083 --> 00:47:32,736
That is due to the anxiety of facing a new experience.

603
00:47:33,482 --> 00:47:38,019
But if that occasion is repeated many times the fear is eliminated.

604
00:47:39,165 --> 00:47:40,957
Original nature can be changed.

605
00:47:41,362 --> 00:47:47,750
It is sufficient as proof to see a Hawa(هوَّا) child, children trained to care for snakes,

606
00:47:47,844 --> 00:47:49,330
 they had these children, who would care for snakes.

607
00:47:50,586 --> 00:47:54,433
Grabbing a large snake that would make a brave man tremble,

608
00:47:55,036 --> 00:47:59,829
while this same child could fear a frog because he is not exposed to frogs.

609
00:48:00,978 --> 00:48:06,436
Taming animals is a process of changing their original nature and it is done through training.

610
00:48:06,962 --> 00:48:11,123
A wolf could play with a sheep, a cat with a mouse, and a dog with a cat,

611
00:48:11,757 --> 00:48:16,681
if they are conditioned to do so, even though that is contrary to their original nature.

612
00:48:17,562 --> 00:48:22,059
Now if animals can change their characteristics can’t humans do the same?

613
00:48:23,959 --> 00:48:26,972
Having a strong heart leads to victory.

614
00:48:27,584 --> 00:48:31,124
Ali(علي) was asked: "How do you defeat your enemies?"

615
00:48:31,393 --> 00:48:34,323
He said: When I would meet my enemy

616
00:48:34,648 --> 00:48:41,968
I would believe with firm conviction that I would defeat him, while he believes that I would defeat him.

617
00:48:42,401 --> 00:48:45,845
So, both myself and his self support me against him.

618
00:48:47,202 --> 00:48:52,897
I mean Ali(علي) starts with confidence that he would defeat the enemy

619
00:48:53,509 --> 00:48:57,609
and the enemy when he hears the name of Ali(علي), he is sure that he's going to lose.

620
00:48:58,345 --> 00:49:03,322
So, Ali(علي)'s heart and the heart of his enemy are both against the enemy.

621
00:49:05,043 --> 00:49:06,606
Half of the battle is already won.

622
00:49:10,227 --> 00:49:16,275
And that's why a Muslim who's willing to die, who's willing to become a Shaheed(شَهِيد), he has already won half of the battle.

623
00:49:17,171 --> 00:49:23,097
And that's why again the Kuffar(كفار) they hate this issue of martyrdom, they hate it, they can't stand it.

624
00:49:23,409 --> 00:49:26,824
They want to change the Fiqh(فقه) of it, they want to change the opinions of the scholars on it.

625
00:49:27,221 --> 00:49:29,634
They don't want any Muslim to do it, at all.

626
00:49:29,919 --> 00:49:33,394
Because that's the one thing that they cannot replicate,

627
00:49:34,926 --> 00:49:40,807
they can meet your weapons with better weapons, they can meet your numbers with more numbers,

628
00:49:41,688 --> 00:49:43,833
they can meet your training with better training,

629
00:49:44,906 --> 00:49:50,418
but they cannot meet a Muslim heart, that is willing to die for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

630
00:49:54,360 --> 00:50:01,108
That is one thing that their best academies, their best training their most advanced weapons cannot deal with.

631
00:50:03,452 --> 00:50:08,086
Some have advised, believe in victory, you will be victorious,

632
00:50:08,586 --> 00:50:14,368
Others say: "If you fear your enemy you have allowed an army to be sent against your heart".

633
00:50:18,035 --> 00:50:19,428
Al-Tartooshi(ألترتوشي) says:

634
00:50:19,799 --> 00:50:21,710
Courage is of three types:

635
00:50:21,902 --> 00:50:31,109
Number 1) A man who stands in front of the army asking for a challenger from the enemy to come out and face him, dueling.

636
00:50:31,654 --> 00:50:39,053
Number 2) A man who remains calm, concentrating, tranquil while the battle is ragging.

637
00:50:39,684 --> 00:50:44,996
And when others are succumbing to fear he has not lost his orientation

638
00:50:45,517 --> 00:50:51,374
and is not confused and acts in a way that proves he has control over himself.

639
00:50:52,409 --> 00:50:59,258
Number 3) A man when everyone else is defeated and is retreating remains firm calling them,

640
00:50:59,552 --> 00:51:01,584
and encouraging them to continue the fight.

641
00:51:01,766 --> 00:51:06,550
Al-Tartooshi(ألترتوشي) says that the third man possesses the greatest form of courage.

642
00:51:07,471 --> 00:51:12,124
He is so courageous that even when everybody else is retreating, he is still firm.

643
00:51:13,088 --> 00:51:15,106
And he's encouraging others to fight.

644
00:51:16,373 --> 00:51:20,842
Then Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) goes through some of the courageous of the Ummah(امة).

645
00:51:22,366 --> 00:51:27,625
I don't think I translated the stories of all of them, those who whatever, I have here.

646
00:51:29,389 --> 00:51:33,150
The most courageous of all mankind is Rasool Allah ﷺ.

647
00:51:33,659 --> 00:51:35,165
He had the strongest heart of all.

648
00:51:36,611 --> 00:51:39,327
He faced the toughest of situations.

649
00:51:39,914 --> 00:51:42,790
Heroes would scatter from around him while he is firm.

650
00:51:43,438 --> 00:51:46,901
The Messenger of Allah never turned his back in battle.

651
00:51:48,044 --> 00:51:52,267
In Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم) Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) narrates:

652
00:51:52,671 --> 00:51:57,326
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the best of people, he was the most generous and the most courageous.

653
00:51:58,912 --> 00:52:04,727
Ali(علي) said: When the ferocity of combat would reach its limit

654
00:52:05,282 --> 00:52:10,721
and the eyes would turn red, we would seek refuge next to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

655
00:52:11,425 --> 00:52:13,631
He would be the closest of us to the enemy.

656
00:52:15,600 --> 00:52:21,042
A man asked Al Bar'a Bin Azib(ألبراءبن عازب): Did you run away during the life of Rasool Ullah?

657
00:52:21,676 --> 00:52:23,694
He said: We did, but he didn’t.

658
00:52:24,717 --> 00:52:26,165
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

659
00:52:27,407 --> 00:52:32,466
In Uhud(أحَد) Obaeye Bin Khalaf(أبي بن خلف), riding his horse, charged towards Rasool Allah ﷺ.

660
00:52:33,215 --> 00:52:37,886
Some Muslims wanted to get in the way to protect Rasool Ullah, but he told them to move aside.

661
00:52:39,480 --> 00:52:46,974
Rasool Allah ﷺ picked up a spear and threw it at Obaeye(اُبَيئ), who was covered in iron armor from head to toe.

662
00:52:47,932 --> 00:52:51,811
Nothing appeared from him except his eyes and a small opening in his neck.

663
00:52:52,716 --> 00:52:56,506
The spear hit him right in the neck and he fell off his horse.

664
00:52:57,152 --> 00:53:02,234
Even though the spear only caused a minor bruise in his neck due to the protection of the armor,

665
00:53:02,772 --> 00:53:06,257
Obaeye(اُبَيئ) rushed back screaming: Muhammad(محمد) has killed me!, Muhammad(محمد) has killed me!

666
00:53:08,367 --> 00:53:12,272
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) checked him and said: We don’t find any major injury, you are fine!

667
00:53:12,629 --> 00:53:17,454
He said: Muhammad(محمد) claimed he would kill me, therefore it must come to happen!.

668
00:53:17,732 --> 00:53:22,626
In other narration, he says that Muhammad(محمد) has claimed that he would kill me and this was in Makkah.

669
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:27,252
Muhammad(محمد) claimed he would kill me, so even if he would have spit on me I would have died.

670
00:53:29,385 --> 00:53:34,331
Obaeye(اُبَيئ) later died on his way back to Makkah, just died out of fear.

671
00:53:43,307 --> 00:53:45,678
The courageous of this Ummah(امة) are too many to count.

672
00:53:46,229 --> 00:53:49,385
On top of the list are the Sahabah(صحابه) whom Allah praised in Qur'an:

673
00:53:49,801 --> 00:53:55,765
Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah, and those with him are forceful against the disbelievers, merciful among themselves.

674
00:53:56,288 --> 00:53:59,328
Among the famous brave men of the Ummah(امة) are: Number 1) Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

675
00:54:02,550 --> 00:54:06,379
I don't know why but apparently some people have developed

676
00:54:07,364 --> 00:54:13,662
a certain mental image of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه that he is very soft man.

677
00:54:15,582 --> 00:54:19,153
Which is contrary to the reality of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

678
00:54:19,391 --> 00:54:24,505
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه could be the firmest, and the toughest.

679
00:54:25,185 --> 00:54:28,687
When the situation demands that position.

680
00:54:30,187 --> 00:54:34,487
In fact he was firmer than Umar(عُمَر) it came to the fighting of Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

681
00:54:34,988 --> 00:54:37,110
When it came to sending the army of Osama(أسامة).

682
00:54:37,451 --> 00:54:43,130
He grabs Umar(عمر), imagine of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who's closer to being short in height.

683
00:54:44,126 --> 00:54:48,872
While Umar(عُمَر) who was a giant Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is grabbing him by the beard and saying,

684
00:54:49,348 --> 00:54:54,016
يا عمر جبَّار في الجاهلية خوارٌ في الإسلام

685
00:54:54,286 --> 00:54:58,809
O Umar(عُمَر), you were a strong man in Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) and now you became a weak man in Islam.

686
00:55:00,341 --> 00:55:05,761
You asked me to keep in, an army that was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

687
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:12,188
Yani(يعني) in fact, even some of the non Muslim tribes had that reputation.

688
00:55:13,069 --> 00:55:16,870
That's how they saw Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) so they said,

689
00:55:17,870 --> 00:55:23,864
see  Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), the name of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the father of Bakr(بكر), Bakr(بكر) is a young lively camel.

690
00:55:24,461 --> 00:55:27,340
A young lively camel that's full of vigor is called Bakr(بكر).

691
00:55:29,261 --> 00:55:32,356
They would make fun of a Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) when he become Khalifah(خليفه) because there was money involved,

692
00:55:32,396 --> 00:55:34,546
they didn't want to pay the Zakah(زکواة), they were paying it to Rasool Ullah.

693
00:55:34,586 --> 00:55:37,031
But now when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)  become Khalifah(خليفه), they don't want to pay him.

694
00:55:37,547 --> 00:55:40,587
They said: We're not going to pay it to Abul Faseel(أبوالفصيل).

695
00:55:41,428 --> 00:55:48,293
We're not going to give it to the father of the infant camel, so they're making fun of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

696
00:55:48,856 --> 00:55:54,646
Udaye Bin Hatim(عدي بن حاتم) told them: A day will come when you will realize that he is Abul Fahal Al-Akbar(أبوالفهل ألأكبر).

697
00:55:55,194 --> 00:55:58,238
You will come to realize that he is the father of the great stallion.

698
00:55:59,819 --> 00:56:04,026
Beware, and the words of Odaye(عدي) came to be true.

699
00:56:04,827 --> 00:56:09,416
The most violent of wars, ever maybe in the history of a Sahabah(صحابه)

700
00:56:09,905 --> 00:56:12,719
occurred under the hands of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) against the Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

701
00:56:13,416 --> 00:56:16,584
Some of them were thrown in wells.

702
00:56:17,265 --> 00:56:19,882
Some of them were thrown from cliffs.

703
00:56:20,257 --> 00:56:21,902
Some of them were burnt in fire.

704
00:56:22,132 --> 00:56:24,549
Some of them were pierced with arrows.

705
00:56:25,156 --> 00:56:29,386
He used all of these brutal ways of executing them

706
00:56:29,426 --> 00:56:32,108
because of the Riddah(ردَّة) and the great crime that they have committed.

707
00:56:33,037 --> 00:56:35,235
And that was done by Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

708
00:56:35,799 --> 00:56:38,653
So he completely changed what they thought of him.

709
00:56:39,589 --> 00:56:46,976
In fact, one of these tribes, they came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and they said we want to make peace with you.

710
00:56:47,999 --> 00:56:49,437
He said: I have two options for you.

711
00:56:50,858 --> 00:56:53,876
فأما الحرب المجلية أو الخطة المخزية

712
00:56:54,717 --> 00:56:59,361
Either a war of extermination, or a humiliating deal.

713
00:56:59,861 --> 00:57:03,901
These are the right, we know what the war of extermination means, that means you're gonna behead us all.

714
00:57:04,274 --> 00:57:07,216
What does a humiliating, to you means.

715
00:57:07,581 --> 00:57:14,266
He said: That you hand over all of your arms and you follow the tails of your camels.

716
00:57:15,176 --> 00:57:22,538
You see, in those days, a man without his weapons is not very different than his camel.

717
00:57:24,506 --> 00:57:28,269
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: You hand over all of your arms and you follow the tails of your camels,

718
00:57:28,409 --> 00:57:29,877
you become equal with your camels.

719
00:57:31,371 --> 00:57:37,991
And you publicly state that anyone who was killed among you is going to hellfire

720
00:57:38,224 --> 00:57:40,380
and anyone who was killed among us goes to Jannah(جنة),

721
00:57:41,674 --> 00:57:49,387
and you pay for the ones you killed among us, and we're not going to pay you anything for the ones killed among you,

722
00:57:50,887 --> 00:57:54,088
and you'll carry on living in this humiliated state,

723
00:57:54,540 --> 00:58:01,058
until Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ shows his Khalifah(خليفه), Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), something that will make him change his mind about it.

724
00:58:04,262 --> 00:58:07,592
So it's an indefinite thing until I change my mind.

725
00:58:08,449 --> 00:58:09,783
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said.

726
00:58:10,831 --> 00:58:15,193
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is listening to this, and he is happy! He said:

727
00:58:15,704 --> 00:58:20,723
When you say that they should give up their weapons and follow their camels I agree.

728
00:58:21,629 --> 00:58:24,589
When you say that they should say that the ones killed among us go to Jannah(جنة),

729
00:58:24,875 --> 00:58:28,393
and the ones who are killed among them go to Naar(ألنار), I agree!

730
00:58:29,099 --> 00:58:35,242
But when you say that they should pay for the ones they killed among us why we don't pay them,

731
00:58:35,488 --> 00:58:41,183
I would disagree with that, because the ones who are killed among us are not killed, they are Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

732
00:58:41,469 --> 00:58:44,183
Therefore we don't take any blood money for them.

733
00:58:46,207 --> 00:58:48,000
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) agreed with what Umar(عُمَر) said.

734
00:58:48,746 --> 00:58:53,218
And they had to accept this humiliating deal they had to.

735
00:58:54,718 --> 00:58:57,395
Otherwise, the other option would be to exterminate them all.

736
00:59:00,892 --> 00:59:04,205
The courage of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was witnessed by the hero of the Ummah(امة),

737
00:59:04,357 --> 00:59:06,056
the hero of this Ummah(امة) is Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

738
00:59:07,929 --> 00:59:11,443
When he was the Khalifah(خليفه). Ali(علي) asked: Who is the bravest of men?

739
00:59:11,554 --> 00:59:14,689
So Ali(علي) is standing on the pulpit and is asking everyone. Who's the bravest of men?

740
00:59:15,015 --> 00:59:15,793
They said: You are!

741
00:59:17,269 --> 00:59:20,327
He said: I have never dueled anyone and lost.

742
00:59:20,882 --> 00:59:22,630
But the bravest man is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

743
00:59:23,787 --> 00:59:27,189
During the battle of Badr(بدر) we built a shed for the Messenger of Allah

744
00:59:27,269 --> 00:59:30,975
and we asked who would be the bodyguard of the Rasool Ullah therein.

745
00:59:31,444 --> 00:59:36,133
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came carrying his sword and defended Rasool Allah ﷺ for the entire day.

746
00:59:37,190 --> 00:59:40,779
In Makkah the disbelievers attacked the Messenger of Allah,

747
00:59:41,285 --> 00:59:44,562
One would pull him, the other would beat him and they would say:

748
00:59:44,976 --> 00:59:46,881
Have you made the gods, one God?

749
00:59:47,554 --> 00:59:51,061
No one dared to go near to Rasool Allah ﷺ except Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

750
00:59:52,059 --> 00:59:55,058
He went and started fighting them and would say:

751
00:59:55,431 --> 00:59:57,868
أن تقتلون رجل أن يقول ربي الله

752
00:59:58,113 --> 01:00:01,669
Are you going to kill a man just because he says: Allah is my Lord!

753
01:00:02,264 --> 01:00:03,226
Then Ali(علي) asked:

754
01:00:04,370 --> 01:00:08,419
Who is better Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) or the believer of the family of Firaun(فرعون)?

755
01:00:08,459 --> 01:00:10,445
Momin Aal Firaun(مؤمن الفرعون) in Surat Ghafir(سورة الغافر).

756
01:00:10,977 --> 01:00:12,247
There is long story about him.

757
01:00:12,755 --> 01:00:18,606
A man who was a believer in that environment of Kuffr(كفر), and he concealed his Eeman(ايمان).

758
01:00:20,272 --> 01:00:26,882
So, the status of this man was so great, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ devoted Ayaat(آيات) and Ayaat(آيات) talking about his story.

759
01:00:28,084 --> 01:00:33,630
So Ali(علي) is asking who is greater, the believer of the family of Firaun(فرعون), or Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).?

760
01:00:37,070 --> 01:00:38,498
The people remained quite.

761
01:00:38,832 --> 01:00:40,804
He said: Why don’t you answer?

762
01:00:42,130 --> 01:00:46,331
In the name of Allah, one moment in the life of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

763
01:00:46,550 --> 01:00:51,963
is greater than the entire earth full of the likes of the believer of the family of Firaun(فرعون)!

764
01:00:52,841 --> 01:00:56,691
The believer of the family of Firaun(فرعون) was a man who concealed his faith,

765
01:00:57,254 --> 01:00:59,785
while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was a man who proclaimed his faith

766
01:01:02,064 --> 01:01:04,072
and then Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه cried.

767
01:01:04,739 --> 01:01:08,057
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the bravest man of this Ummah(امة) after Rasool Allah ﷺ.

768
01:01:08,580 --> 01:01:14,412
One can note the strength of his heart during the battle of Badr(بدر), Uhud(أحَد), Khandaq(خندق), Hudaybiyah(حديبية), and Hunain(حنين).

769
01:01:15,118 --> 01:01:20,337
It is enough to note his steadfastness, firmness, and strengthening of the entire Ummah(امة)

770
01:01:20,713 --> 01:01:25,492
when the greatest disaster of all befell us, is the death of Muhammadﷺ.

771
01:01:26,223 --> 01:01:30,520
That was when the hearts deviated, and the nation was shaken.

772
01:01:31,131 --> 01:01:35,149
When all the hearts where trembling the heart of As-Sidique(ألصديق) was firm.

773
01:01:36,443 --> 01:01:39,499
If the heart of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was placed on one side of the scale

774
01:01:39,905 --> 01:01:45,173
and the hearts of all the Ummah(امة) on the other, his heart would outweigh them all.

775
01:01:45,776 --> 01:01:49,204
The courage of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in his decision to fight the apostates,

776
01:01:49,666 --> 01:01:56,372
if distributed over the hearts of the cowards on the entire face of the earth, it would be sufficient to make them brave.

777
01:01:58,874 --> 01:02:01,320
So you can see that the issue with courage is in the heart,

778
01:02:01,400 --> 01:02:10,614
because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), in terms of his physical stature, was extremely, he was very thin.

779
01:02:13,342 --> 01:02:20,606
He was so thin that he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ complaining that his Izaar(إزار) wouldn't hold on to his waist.

780
01:02:21,521 --> 01:02:24,778
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said that you should have your Izaar(إزار) above the ankle.

781
01:02:25,556 --> 01:02:27,144
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he said:

782
01:02:27,675 --> 01:02:30,536
إنَّا إزاري لا تمسك على حقوي

783
01:02:30,589 --> 01:02:36,577
My Izaar(إزار) wouldn't hold on to my waist he was so slim, that his Izaar(إزار) would keep on falling.

784
01:02:36,657 --> 01:02:39,720
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had to keep on pulling it up.

785
01:02:40,569 --> 01:02:42,435
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر):

786
01:02:42,515 --> 01:02:43,196
لست منهم

787
01:02:43,236 --> 01:02:45,999
You're not one of those who are doing it out of pride.

788
01:02:46,714 --> 01:02:50,317
He was so slim, it says: You could see the bones on his face.

789
01:02:51,301 --> 01:02:52,532
Number 2) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

790
01:02:52,972 --> 01:02:58,239
It is sufficient to point out that the courage of Umar(عُمَر) was sufficient enough to make Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) avoid him.

791
01:02:58,594 --> 01:02:59,301
That's enough!

792
01:02:59,959 --> 01:03:01,367
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

793
01:03:01,856 --> 01:03:14,039
ما لَقِيَكَ الشَّيْطانُ قَطُّ سالِكًا فَجًّا إلَّا سَلَكَ فَجًّا غيرَ فَجِّكَ

794
01:03:15,692 --> 01:03:20,227
When Umar(عُمَر) would be walking down the road and Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) sees him, He would take another road.

795
01:03:22,675 --> 01:03:30,072
The reason is Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) knows it's a waste of time, to try to deal with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

796
01:03:30,231 --> 01:03:31,572
You can't change anything in him.

797
01:03:32,279 --> 01:03:36,207
So he fears him so much and he is frustrated with him so much and he just gave up on him,

798
01:03:36,596 --> 01:03:38,654
he would leave him alone and go another way.

799
01:03:41,015 --> 01:03:42,287
The Messenger of Allah told Umar(عُمَر):

800
01:03:42,327 --> 01:03:47,207
O son of Khattab(خطاب), In the name of whom my soul is in His hands whenever Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) sees you taking a route,

801
01:03:47,576 --> 01:03:48,314
he would take another.

802
01:03:48,639 --> 01:03:49,762
That’s in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

803
01:03:50,377 --> 01:03:52,441
His Islam brought strength to the Muslims.

804
01:03:52,735 --> 01:03:54,147
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said:

805
01:03:54,441 --> 01:03:58,994
We used to not be able to pray next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) publicly until Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim.

806
01:04:00,591 --> 01:04:02,091
Number 3: Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب):

807
01:04:02,512 --> 01:04:07,341
He was the lion of this Ummah(امة), he never missed a battle with Rasool Allah ﷺ except Tabook(تبوک)

808
01:04:07,826 --> 01:04:11,387
because Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed him over Madina in his absence.

809
01:04:12,136 --> 01:04:14,771
During the battle of Khaybar(خَيْبَر), Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

810
01:04:15,370 --> 01:04:21,726
Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him.

811
01:04:22,821 --> 01:04:28,101
He does not turn his back away in battle and Allah will make opening occur on his hands.

812
01:04:28,385 --> 01:04:30,488
All of the Sahabah(صحابه) desired that honor.

813
01:04:30,908 --> 01:04:36,518
The next day, so the Sahabah(صحابه) woke up very early in the morning and they started walking in front of Rasool Ullah,

814
01:04:36,939 --> 01:04:38,399
so that he will choose them.

815
01:04:39,248 --> 01:04:41,455
The next day the Messenger of Allah called Ali(علي).

816
01:04:41,867 --> 01:04:47,231
They told them Ali(علي), Ali(علي) was suffering, his eyes were suffering and couldn't see that day.

817
01:04:47,761 --> 01:04:50,300
So he told Rasool Allah ﷺ that he cannot see.

818
01:04:50,340 --> 01:04:51,749
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Call him,

819
01:04:52,205 --> 01:04:55,184
and Rasool Allah ﷺ spit in his eyes and he was immediately cured,

820
01:04:55,641 --> 01:04:56,728
and he gave him the banner.

821
01:04:56,958 --> 01:04:58,538
Musab Ibn Zubair(مصعب إبن زبير) said:

822
01:04:58,871 --> 01:05:01,125
Ali(علي) was very cautious in battle.

823
01:05:01,617 --> 01:05:06,720
Even though Ali(علي) was courageous but his courage, doesn't mean that you're not cautious,

824
01:05:07,005 --> 01:05:08,983
courage doesn't mean that you become reckless.

825
01:05:10,220 --> 01:05:15,971
Musab Ibn Zubair(مصعب إبن زبير) said: Ali(علي) was very cautious in battle.

826
01:05:16,487 --> 01:05:24,427
He was swerve terrifically from his enemy and whenever he charges his enemy he would protect all his sides

827
01:05:24,807 --> 01:05:30,100
and when he retreats back from his charge he would be even more protective of himself.

828
01:05:30,721 --> 01:05:32,087
No one could get to him.

829
01:05:33,777 --> 01:05:35,890
His shield was one sided.

830
01:05:36,070 --> 01:05:38,356
It only protected him from the front.

831
01:05:38,797 --> 01:05:41,884
When asked: Don’t you fear an attack from behind?

832
01:05:41,964 --> 01:05:46,051
He replied: I never give my enemy the chance to attack me from my back.

833
01:05:48,728 --> 01:05:50,999
So he didn't really needed a shield from behind.

834
01:05:53,704 --> 01:05:55,394
Number 4) Talha Bin Ubaidellah(طلحة بن عبيدالله):

835
01:05:56,179 --> 01:05:58,920
He is one of the ten given the glad tidings of Paradise.

836
01:05:59,687 --> 01:06:06,033
During Uhud(أحَد), he shielded Rasool Allah ﷺ with his own body causing over 70 injuries in his body.

837
01:06:06,736 --> 01:06:09,905
Whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to look at the disbelievers,

838
01:06:10,220 --> 01:06:14,767
Talha(طلحة) would plead with him not to do so and would shield him with his body.

839
01:06:17,307 --> 01:06:19,411
Number 5) Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام):

840
01:06:20,037 --> 01:06:23,498
He is also one of the ten given the glad tidings of Paradise.

841
01:06:23,852 --> 01:06:26,273
He was the first Muslim to draw out a sword.

842
01:06:26,868 --> 01:06:31,137
During the early days of Islam in Makkah a rumor spread that Rasool Allah ﷺ was kidnapped.

843
01:06:31,943 --> 01:06:35,277
Zubair(زبير) drew out his sword and went looking for him.

844
01:06:35,673 --> 01:06:37,943
He ran into Rasool Allah ﷺ who asked him:

845
01:06:38,221 --> 01:06:39,679
What’s wrong with you Zubair?

846
01:06:39,956 --> 01:06:43,734
He said: I heard that you were kidnapped so I came out to fight them!

847
01:06:44,051 --> 01:06:45,408
Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed for him.

848
01:06:45,623 --> 01:06:49,816
And we talked about the story with the spear, when he bent the blade,

849
01:06:50,076 --> 01:06:57,875
and did I say when he chopped the, the Kafir(كافر) with the sword and it split the saddle.

850
01:06:58,621 --> 01:07:06,937
In one of the battles, Az-Zubair(ألزبير) hits this enemy soldier who was on his horse.

851
01:07:07,579 --> 01:07:12,428
He hit him so hard that he split him into two.

852
01:07:14,395 --> 01:07:19,439
Not only that but the sword went down a bit further, and cut the saddle.

853
01:07:20,196 --> 01:07:22,221
So the saddle fell from both sides.

854
01:07:22,920 --> 01:07:25,601
Sahabah(صحابه), they saw that and they were so impressed they said:

855
01:07:26,094 --> 01:07:27,903
This is a very, very sharp sword.

856
01:07:28,634 --> 01:07:29,925
This is a powerful sword.

857
01:07:30,381 --> 01:07:33,863
He said: It's not the sword, but it's the arm that's carrying the sword.

858
01:07:34,579 --> 01:07:36,604
Don't give credit to my sword.

859
01:07:44,199 --> 01:07:46,141
Number 6) Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص):

860
01:07:46,696 --> 01:07:49,394
He is one of ten given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

861
01:07:49,871 --> 01:07:55,354
Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed for him: O Allah make his arrow hit its target and make his prayer accepted.

862
01:07:56,013 --> 01:07:58,434
Umar(عُمَر) appointed him to lead the army at Qadisiyah(قادسية).

863
01:07:58,474 --> 01:08:01,802
The Muslims won and he continued leading them in Persia until he opened most of it

864
01:08:02,239 --> 01:08:04,061
and entered the capital, Al-Mada'in(ألمدائن).

865
01:08:04,526 --> 01:08:07,558
Saad(سعد) is the one who founded the two cities of Kufa(كوفة) and Basra(بصرى).

866
01:08:08,193 --> 01:08:09,884
He is the one who founded them.

867
01:08:10,875 --> 01:08:17,711
When he was dying he requested his body be rapped and buried in an old wool cloth.

868
01:08:18,183 --> 01:08:25,034
He said: This was what I had on me, during the battle of Badr(بدر) and I’ve reserved it for this day.

869
01:08:26,510 --> 01:08:28,295
Number 7. Abu Obaidah Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدة بن جرَّاح):

870
01:08:28,685 --> 01:08:31,026
He is one of the ten given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

871
01:08:31,359 --> 01:08:33,548
Umar(عُمَر) appointed him over the army opening Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

872
01:08:33,588 --> 01:08:35,985
He was the leader of the army during the great battle of Yarmuk(يرموك).

873
01:08:36,341 --> 01:08:38,468
He died in the plague of Amawas(عمواس) in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

874
01:08:39,349 --> 01:08:41,822
Number 8) Hamza Bin AbdulMutalib(حمزة بن عبدالمطلب):

875
01:08:42,082 --> 01:08:44,121
He is the lion of Allah and His Messenger.

876
01:08:44,693 --> 01:08:50,094
After the battle of Badr(بدر), Umayyah Bin Khalaf(أمية بن خلف), who was captured asked Abdul Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

877
01:08:50,427 --> 01:08:54,961
Who was the man in your army marked with an ostrich feather on his chest?

878
01:08:56,166 --> 01:08:57,914
Abdul Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: That is Hamza(حمزه).

879
01:08:58,438 --> 01:09:01,692
Umayyah(أمية) said: He is the one, who brought ruin to us!

880
01:09:03,049 --> 01:09:04,715
He was killed during the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

881
01:09:05,152 --> 01:09:07,264
Number 9): Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفرإبن أبي طالب):

882
01:09:07,993 --> 01:09:10,059
He was ten years older than his brother Ali(علي).

883
01:09:10,493 --> 01:09:12,908
He was the second leader in line at the battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

884
01:09:13,262 --> 01:09:17,908
When he took over after Zaid(زيد), he carried the banner with his right hand which was cut off

885
01:09:17,948 --> 01:09:24,467
so he carried it with his left, which was in turn also cut off so he embraced the banner and continued fighting until he fell.

886
01:09:24,832 --> 01:09:27,685
They found in the front of his body over 90 injuries.

887
01:09:28,570 --> 01:09:30,529
10. Muadh Bin Amr Bin Jamooh(معاذبن عمرو بن جموح):

888
01:09:30,904 --> 01:09:36,714
He was the slayer of the Pharaoh of this Ummah(امة) Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

889
01:09:37,991 --> 01:09:41,398
He said: I made Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) my target on the day of Badr(بدر).

890
01:09:41,917 --> 01:09:46,663
When I found him I charged at him and struck him with my sword and cut his leg in two.

891
01:09:47,338 --> 01:09:51,409
Then his son Ikrimah(عكرمة) hit me on my shoulder until he cut off my arm.

892
01:09:52,305 --> 01:09:56,017
It only remained hanging to my body by the skin of my side.

893
01:09:56,766 --> 01:10:01,545
But because fighting distracted me, I remained dragging it behind me for most of the day.

894
01:10:02,481 --> 01:10:06,122
When it annoyed me I placed my foot over it and pulled it off.

895
01:10:08,249 --> 01:10:09,844
11) Al-Baraa Bin Malik(ألبراء بن مالك):

896
01:10:13,130 --> 01:10:15,814
He is the brother of Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) the servant of Rasool Ullah,

897
01:10:16,457 --> 01:10:18,012
he was one of heroes of this Ummah(امة).

898
01:10:18,734 --> 01:10:22,413
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) heard his brother Al-Baraa(ألبراء) humming poetry so he told him:

899
01:10:22,453 --> 01:10:25,227
O my brother! Are you are humming poetry?

900
01:10:25,735 --> 01:10:27,940
What if this is the last thing you speak?

901
01:10:30,132 --> 01:10:32,413
He said: No!

902
01:10:32,984 --> 01:10:39,495
A man like me won't die on his bed, I’ve killed ninety nine of the nonbelievers and hypocrites!

903
01:10:40,222 --> 01:10:41,468
Sunan Ibn Abi Shaiba(مصنف إبن أبي شيبة).

904
01:10:41,595 --> 01:10:47,782
Umar(عُمَر) wrote to his military generals to never allow Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) to hold any position of leadership in the Muslim armies.

905
01:10:47,862 --> 01:10:51,522
The reason: Umar(عُمَر) said: He is too hazardous for the Muslims!

906
01:10:53,227 --> 01:10:54,001
That's in Al-Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

907
01:10:54,286 --> 01:10:56,942
During the battle against the forces of Musailima(مسيلمة), the liar,

908
01:10:57,231 --> 01:11:00,756
he sat on a shield and asked the Muslims to carry the shield on their spears

909
01:11:01,199 --> 01:11:04,927
and throw him over the walls of the enemy in order to open the gates!

910
01:11:05,095 --> 01:11:08,730
He did open the gates but after he received over 80 injuries.

911
01:11:08,841 --> 01:11:09,807
That’s in Asabah(أثابة).

912
01:11:11,823 --> 01:11:18,331
On the day of the battle of Tastur(تستر) the Muslims asked Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) to make an oath to give them victory.

913
01:11:18,641 --> 01:11:22,077
 Because Al-Bara'a(ألبراء), was one of the men intended by the Hadith(حديث),

914
01:11:22,172 --> 01:11:26,277
رب أشعث أغبر لو أقسم على الله لَأَبَرَّهُ

915
01:11:27,065 --> 01:11:34,220
There is a man with untidy hair, and very dusty clothes.

916
01:11:35,212 --> 01:11:37,815
But if he makes an oath, Allah will fulfill it.

917
01:11:39,149 --> 01:11:46,508
A very simple man, poor, but Allah loves that man so much, if that man makes an oath, Allah will make it happen.

918
01:11:48,342 --> 01:11:51,824
So they told Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) ask Allah to give us victory.

919
01:11:51,864 --> 01:11:59,634
He said: O Allah! I make an oath that you hand us over their shoulders and to make me follow your prophet.

920
01:12:00,564 --> 01:12:02,754
He charged the enemy and the Muslims followed him.

921
01:12:03,024 --> 01:12:07,471
The Persians lost, and Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) was martyred, Allah fulfilled his oath.

922
01:12:08,392 --> 01:12:11,780
Anas(أنس) narrated: When Abu Musa(أبوموسى) was appointed governor over Basra(ألبصرى),

923
01:12:12,240 --> 01:12:17,112
he told Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) to choose any position of leadership in his government, and he will be appointed to it.

924
01:12:17,462 --> 01:12:19,031
 Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) said: I don’t want any.

925
01:12:19,644 --> 01:12:26,845
Rather I want you to hand me over my bow, horse, spear, sword, and shield and then sent me to Jihad(جهاد).

926
01:12:27,134 --> 01:12:29,872
He sent him in an army Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) was the first to die.

927
01:12:31,420 --> 01:12:34,803
12. Samaak Bin Kharshah Abu Dujana(سماك بن خرشة ابودجانة),

928
01:12:36,189 --> 01:12:40,744
Before the battle of Uhud(أحَد) started the Messenger of Allah held a sword in his hand and said:

929
01:12:41,077 --> 01:12:44,137
Who would fight with this sword and give it its due right?

930
01:12:45,756 --> 01:12:50,974
Some men stood up and offered to take it but Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t give it to them.

931
01:12:51,292 --> 01:12:55,524
And then Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) stood up and said: O Rasool Allah ﷺ what is its due right?

932
01:12:56,238 --> 01:13:00,386
He said: That you strike with it the faces of the enemy until it bends!

933
01:13:01,545 --> 01:13:04,870
Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) said: I will take it, O Rasool Ullah, he gave it to him.

934
01:13:05,569 --> 01:13:06,826
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) said:

935
01:13:06,866 --> 01:13:12,165
I felt saddened that I, the cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ, would ask for the sword and would not get it

936
01:13:12,785 --> 01:13:14,147
but Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) would.

937
01:13:15,238 --> 01:13:18,577
So I decided to follow Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) and see what he would do with it.

938
01:13:19,421 --> 01:13:24,269
Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) pulled out a Red Bandana and tied it around his head.

939
01:13:25,085 --> 01:13:29,364
The Ansaar(أنصار) said: Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) has pulled out his Bandana of death!

940
01:13:30,013 --> 01:13:34,415
He then attacked enemy and whenever he would face anyone he would kill him!

941
01:13:35,086 --> 01:13:38,123
Before the battle he marched with pride before the enemy.

942
01:13:38,690 --> 01:13:41,927
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is a walk despised by Allah,

943
01:13:42,500 --> 01:13:44,905
because he walked with pride.

944
01:13:45,350 --> 01:13:52,483
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is the walk despised by Allah except in this situation.

945
01:13:52,686 --> 01:13:55,584
This is stiking fear in the hearts of the enemy.

946
01:13:57,151 --> 01:14:02,182
During the battle of Al-Yamamah(أليمامة), he threw himself over the wall surrounding the city and broke his leg.

947
01:14:02,664 --> 01:14:05,967
He continued fighting with a broken leg until he became Shaheed(شهيد).

948
01:14:07,157 --> 01:14:08,182
13. Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

949
01:14:08,629 --> 01:14:10,462
He is the drawn sword of Allah.

950
01:14:11,161 --> 01:14:16,166
As soon as he became Muslim, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sending him to fight the enemies of Allah.

951
01:14:16,692 --> 01:14:19,258
Khalid(خالد) never in his life lost a battle.

952
01:14:19,679 --> 01:14:20,864
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said:

953
01:14:21,383 --> 01:14:28,004
If I were to marry a beautiful woman whom I love, or if I were given the good news of having a newborn son,

954
01:14:28,490 --> 01:14:36,009
is less beloved and dear to my heart then to be in a cold icy night, in an army waiting to meet my enemy the next morning.

955
01:14:36,426 --> 01:14:38,400
I advise you to go on Jihad(جهاد).

956
01:14:38,650 --> 01:14:40,730
These were the last words of Khalid(خالد).

957
01:14:42,272 --> 01:14:44,022
Salamah Bin Akwa(سلمةبن أكوع) Number 14),

958
01:14:45,144 --> 01:14:48,455
We mentioned his story earlier when he fought the disbelievers alone.

959
01:14:49,307 --> 01:14:51,300
Rasool Allah ﷺ said about him on that day.

960
01:14:51,524 --> 01:14:55,068
The best of our foot soldiers today is Salamah Bin Akwa(سلمةبن أكوع).

961
01:14:55,615 --> 01:14:57,851
Number 15) Ukasha Bin Mahsan(عكاشة بن محصن),

962
01:14:58,483 --> 01:15:00,212
His bravery in war was well known,

963
01:15:00,574 --> 01:15:06,528
in the battle of Ghabah(غبَّة) he saw Amr Bin Abaar(عمروبن عبار) along with his father riding the same camel.

964
01:15:06,769 --> 01:15:10,182
He threw his spear and killed them both, the same time.

965
01:15:11,098 --> 01:15:15,571
Two men riding on a camel struck them with the spear and killed both.

966
01:15:16,675 --> 01:15:18,894
16. Amr Bin Madi Yakrib(عمروبن معديكرب):

967
01:15:20,204 --> 01:15:22,927
He was a king from Yemen who was famous for his bravery.

968
01:15:23,345 --> 01:15:27,663
He later embraced Islam, Umar(عُمَر) would count him as a thousand men.

969
01:15:28,439 --> 01:15:30,421
Al-Tartushi(ألترتوشي) mentions in Siraj Ul Muluk(سراج الملوك)

970
01:15:30,501 --> 01:15:34,503
that Amr Bin Madi Yakrib(عمروبن معديكرب) went next to the river and told his people:

971
01:15:34,937 --> 01:15:40,436
I am going to cross the bridge, if you follow me after a time equivalent to the time it takes to slaughter a camel.

972
01:15:40,898 --> 01:15:46,413
You would find me with my sword in my hand fighting whoever is in front of me with the enemy surrounding me

973
01:15:46,453 --> 01:15:47,791
and I am standing between them.

974
01:15:48,130 --> 01:15:50,395
If you come later than that you would find me dead.

975
01:15:51,232 --> 01:15:54,198
He then crossed the bridge over the river towards the enemy’s camp.

976
01:15:54,658 --> 01:15:57,464
A while later his people said: O sons of Zabid(زبيد)!

977
01:15:57,731 --> 01:15:59,196
Are we going to leave our man alone?

978
01:15:59,477 --> 01:16:00,913
We might not even catch him alive.

979
01:16:01,447 --> 01:16:04,205
So they crossed the bridge and found him without his horse,

980
01:16:04,515 --> 01:16:08,880
while he was holding both back legs of an enemy’s horse and the horse failed to move.

981
01:16:10,503 --> 01:16:15,163
The fighter on the horse was trying to reach Amr(عمرو) behind him, with his sword with no avail.

982
01:16:15,848 --> 01:16:23,767
I mean, you can imagine, he is frantically trying to hit Amr(عمرو) who's holding the horse and the horse cannot move.

983
01:16:23,840 --> 01:16:27,463
 When the fighter saw us attacking he came down from his horse and ran away.

984
01:16:28,443 --> 01:16:34,773
Amr(عمرو) then mounted the horse, he told us, you almost were almost going to miss me.

985
01:16:35,307 --> 01:16:41,068
They asked him: Where is your horse? He said: It was hit by an arrow that killed it and I fell off its back.

986
01:16:42,778 --> 01:16:45,127
17. Ikrimah(عكرمة), the son of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل):

987
01:16:46,780 --> 01:16:51,646
He was courageous before becoming a Muslim and Islam only added to his courage.

988
01:16:52,063 --> 01:16:54,413
During the battle of Yarmuk(يرموك) he fought ferociously.

989
01:16:54,993 --> 01:16:57,482
He was told to slow down and be cautious.

990
01:16:57,522 --> 01:17:04,812
He replied: I used to fight to defend Allaat(علَّات) and Uzza(عُزى) and I would not take any care for myself.

991
01:17:05,383 --> 01:17:08,701
Now you want me to take caution when I am fighting for Allah and His Messenger!

992
01:17:09,233 --> 01:17:11,836
He then said: Who is going to pledge to die!

993
01:17:12,776 --> 01:17:18,501
Al-Harith Bin Hisham(ألحارث بن هشام), Dhirar bin al Azwar(ضرارإبن أزور) along with 400 of the brave gave their pledge.

994
01:17:19,427 --> 01:17:22,445
They attacked the Romans and disappeared in their ranks.

995
01:17:22,801 --> 01:17:24,064
Ikrimah(عكرمة) never came out.

996
01:17:24,183 --> 01:17:26,568
His body was found with more than seventy injuries.

997
01:17:27,179 --> 01:17:32,319
These are 400, who pledged martyrdom, in a martyrdom operation.

998
01:17:34,796 --> 01:17:36,562
18. Tulaiha Al-Azdi(طليحةألأسدي):

999
01:17:38,711 --> 01:17:43,128
When Saad Bin Abi Waqas(سعدبن أبي وقاص) asked the Khalifah(خليفه) Umar(عُمَر) to sent him reinforcement.

1000
01:17:43,973 --> 01:17:46,755
Umar(عُمَر) replied: I have sent you 2000 men.

1001
01:17:47,531 --> 01:17:49,981
Amr Bin Madi Yakrib(عمروبن معديكرب) and Tulaiha Al-Azdi(طليحةألأسدي).

1002
01:17:50,384 --> 01:17:52,057
Each one of them counts as a thousand.

1003
01:17:53,440 --> 01:17:59,636
Tulaiha(طليحة), Amr(عمرو), and Qais Bin Makshooh(قيس بن مكشوح) went on a reconnaissance mission to the enemy’s army.

1004
01:18:00,598 --> 01:18:07,349
Both Amr(عمرو) and Qais(قيس) kidnapped some Persian soldiers and brought them back to the Muslim camp for interrogation.

1005
01:18:08,165 --> 01:18:13,994
Tulaiha(طليحة) went further, so now these were three men, two of them came back with prisoners

1006
01:18:14,284 --> 01:18:15,469
and Tulaiha(طليحة) is carrying on.

1007
01:18:16,458 --> 01:18:20,420
Tulaiha(طليحة) went further until he was in the camp of the army’s commander.

1008
01:18:21,458 --> 01:18:26,973
He hid until nightfall and then went straight to the tent of the commander and took away his horse,

1009
01:18:27,947 --> 01:18:30,211
which was tied to the tent and ran away.

1010
01:18:30,659 --> 01:18:32,931
A Persian horseman saw that and he followed him.

1011
01:18:33,569 --> 01:18:37,914
Tulaiha(طليحة) killed him and took his horse along with his and the commander’s horse.

1012
01:18:38,527 --> 01:18:43,299
Another horseman pursued him and Tulaiha(طليحة) also killed him and took his horse.

1013
01:18:43,806 --> 01:18:46,684
A third horseman attacked him but then surrendered.

1014
01:18:46,991 --> 01:18:53,270
Tulaiha(طليحة) captured him and carried him away, along with a total of four horses in addition to his.

1015
01:18:53,954 --> 01:18:58,504
The Muslim leaders gathered to question the Persian who turned out to be one of their leaders.

1016
01:18:58,570 --> 01:19:03,469
He said: I have fought numerous battles but I have never seen anything like this man!

1017
01:19:04,183 --> 01:19:09,527
He crossed our camps until he made it to where even the bravest of men would not dare,

1018
01:19:09,804 --> 01:19:14,090
the camp of our army’s commander, which had over 70,000 soldiers.

1019
01:19:15,248 --> 01:19:18,809
As if that wasn’t enough he went ahead and took the commander’s horse!

1020
01:19:19,746 --> 01:19:24,738
The first of us to follow him was considered among us to be equal to a thousand men and he killed him!

1021
01:19:25,446 --> 01:19:27,288
The second to follow him was killed

1022
01:19:27,876 --> 01:19:34,627
and then I pursued him and I don’t think that there is anyone in the army equal to myself in strength and courage.

1023
01:19:35,113 --> 01:19:37,329
But I saw death on his hands and surrendered!

1024
01:19:38,459 --> 01:19:41,443
The man then accepted Islam and fought alongside the Muslims.

1025
01:19:44,094 --> 01:19:44,832
This is Da'wah(دعوة)!!!

1026
01:19:52,558 --> 01:19:55,431
19. Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن زبير):

1027
01:19:56,442 --> 01:19:59,800
He was the courageous and son of the courageous.

1028
01:20:00,854 --> 01:20:04,040
You know by the way in Da'wah(دعوة), because

1029
01:20:05,165 --> 01:20:15,166
والأرْواحُ جُنُودٌ مُجَنَّدَةٌ، فَما تَعارَفَ مِنْها ائْتَلَفَ، وما تَناكَرَ مِنْها اخْتَلَفَ

1030
01:20:16,068 --> 01:20:20,206
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that hearts are soldiers of Allah,

1031
01:20:20,786 --> 01:20:28,982
the ones that are similar cling together and the ones that are different, they feel repulsion from each other.

1032
01:20:30,417 --> 01:20:39,651
So, when we give Dawah(دعوة), you tend to attract the people who are similar to you.

1033
01:20:41,828 --> 01:20:48,205
So a brave, courageous man like Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) would attract people who are similar to him.

1034
01:20:49,165 --> 01:20:51,991
There is some attraction because they have something in common.

1035
01:20:54,035 --> 01:21:03,301
While, if weak and feable it would also tend to attract similar people to the religion.

1036
01:21:04,670 --> 01:21:10,083
Now it's all Da'wah(دعوة) everybody, Islam is for everyone, but there is an influence of personality.

1037
01:21:10,559 --> 01:21:13,548
When it comes to the people that would be attract to your Da'wah(دعوة).

1038
01:21:14,838 --> 01:21:17,838
So different people could be given Da'wah(دعوة) to the same person.

1039
01:21:18,948 --> 01:21:23,044
But what he hears from one particular person would be more appealing to his ears and heart

1040
01:21:23,765 --> 01:21:25,243
than what everybody else has to say.

1041
01:21:26,305 --> 01:21:29,440
So there's one scholar who actually said,

1042
01:21:31,336 --> 01:21:38,073
that even if the Muslims are successful in their Da'wah(دعوة) today when they're weak, that weakness would carry on.

1043
01:21:38,598 --> 01:21:44,300
Because whoever would come into the religion would either have similar attributes of weakness

1044
01:21:44,768 --> 01:21:49,491
or would be conditioned to be in that state of weakness because of the state of the Ummah(امة).

1045
01:21:52,745 --> 01:21:57,943
Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن زبير), he was the courageous and son of the courageous, his father was Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام).

1046
01:21:58,227 --> 01:22:03,432
Abdullah(عبدالله) participated in the opening of North Africa and killed Jarjeer(جرجير), the king of the Berber.

1047
01:22:03,877 --> 01:22:05,450
20. Abdullah Bin Abi Sarh(عبدالله بن أبي سرح):

1048
01:22:06,131 --> 01:22:12,228
He was the opener of North Africa, he was the one to lead the first naval battle of the Muslims.

1049
01:22:12,474 --> 01:22:17,609
The battle of al Sawari(سواري) against the Romans, he was appointed by Uthman(عثمان) to govern Egypt.

1050
01:22:18,053 --> 01:22:23,124
When the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) occurred he retired to Al-Ramlah(ألرملة) in Falestine(فلسطين) where he remained until he died.

1051
01:22:23,584 --> 01:22:25,083
21. Al Qa'qaa Bin Amr(ألقعقاع بن عمرو),

1052
01:22:25,834 --> 01:22:27,540
Question

1053
01:22:28,354 --> 01:22:30,534
(The Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Ali(علي) and Muawiya(معاويه))

1054
01:22:31,780 --> 01:22:33,152
21. Al Qa'qaa Bin Amr(ألقعقاع بن عمرو),

1055
01:22:33,532 --> 01:22:36,827
When the Messenger of Allah was consulting the Sahabah(صحابه) before Badr(بدر).

1056
01:22:37,061 --> 01:22:42,334
Al Qa'qaa(ألقعقاع) said: Go ahead and fight and we will not say what Banu Israel(بنواسرائيل) said to Musa(موسى),

1057
01:22:42,655 --> 01:22:45,075
Go and fight with your Lord, we will stay here.

1058
01:22:45,409 --> 01:22:49,387
But we will say: Go ahead and fight with your Lord, we are going to fight with you.

1059
01:22:49,860 --> 01:22:54,277
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said about him: The voice of Al Qa'qaa(ألقعقاع) battle is better than 1000 men.

1060
01:22:55,602 --> 01:23:02,958
Can one of you please show me the book that has this part.

1061
01:23:05,955 --> 01:23:09,228
If we see, if that's the last person and he talks about.

1062
01:23:23,756 --> 01:23:29,510
There's Yazeed Bin Muawiya(يزيد بن معاويه), Abu Muhammad Abdullah Bin Batta(أبومحمدعبدالله بن بطال),

1063
01:23:35,620 --> 01:23:38,230
Musa Bin Nusair(موسى بن نُصَير) and Mohalab Bin Ibn Safra(محلب بن أبي صفرة),

1064
01:23:39,136 --> 01:23:42,417
Mua'atism(معتصم) Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), Al-Hadi(ألهادي) Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين).

1065
01:23:42,695 --> 01:23:46,425
This personality unfortunately I didn't translate it.

1066
01:23:46,885 --> 01:23:52,501
But this man is truly phenomenal, Ahmad Bin Is'haaq Al-Bukhari Al-Sarmari(أحمد بن إسحاق ألبخاري ألسرماري).

1067
01:23:54,094 --> 01:23:56,846
Al-Zahid Al-Mujahid Al-Faris Al-Mash'hoor(ألزاهد ألمجاهد ألفارس ألمشهور) Shaikh(شيخ) of Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1068
01:23:56,886 --> 01:24:00,947
He is one of the teachers of Bukhari(بخاريْ), and he's from his land.

1069
01:24:01,270 --> 01:24:04,372
Al-Ahad Shuj'aan Al-Alim(أحد شجعان ألعالم), he's one of the brave men of the world,

1070
01:24:04,951 --> 01:24:11,502
and he is the example, the role model of bravery, and Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ) says,

1071
01:24:12,375 --> 01:24:15,242
ما بلغنا أنه كان في الإسلام ولا في الجاهلية مثله

1072
01:24:15,557 --> 01:24:19,025
We don't know if there's anyone before Islam or after Islam like him.

1073
01:24:19,929 --> 01:24:22,872
This one, was a truly amazing personality.

1074
01:24:23,048 --> 01:24:25,437
ورواة أبن ذهبي الحافظ في تهذيب

1075
01:24:27,849 --> 01:24:37,908
He actually has 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 pages about him.

1076
01:24:38,728 --> 01:24:46,479
I'm very sorry that I didn't translate it, his name is Sarmari(سرماري), Ahmad Ibn Is'haq Al-Sarmari(أحمد بن إسحاق ألسرماري).

1077
01:24:51,433 --> 01:24:59,675
And I remember reading some stuff about him in some other books and it's just amazing and he was also a scholar.

1078
01:25:00,813 --> 01:25:07,931
Brothers we're going to carry on without a break, because we have a lot of material to cover, so be alert.

1079
01:25:09,450 --> 01:25:12,983
This is our last session, still have two chapters to go.

1080
01:25:14,471 --> 01:25:18,576
We have the heavy duty chapter of necessary rulings for the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) to know Fiqh(فقه).

1081
01:25:18,822 --> 01:25:19,822
Fiqh(فقه)

1082
01:25:20,377 --> 01:25:23,402
Some legal rulings regarding Jihad(جهاد):

1083
01:25:25,227 --> 01:25:30,394
The body of knowledge is immense, and the details of rulings are endless.

1084
01:25:31,371 --> 01:25:35,991
But no one is excused from learning at least the fundamentals.

1085
01:25:39,662 --> 01:25:44,074
It is compulsory on every Muslim to learn the necessary knowledge

1086
01:25:44,439 --> 01:25:49,297
and that is the knowledge which the validity of our actions depends on.

1087
01:25:51,183 --> 01:25:53,935
So these are the necessary Ahkam(أحكام) to know.

1088
01:25:58,229 --> 01:26:04,213
Following are issues, which are necessary for the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) to learn for their Jihad(جهاد) to be acceptable.

1089
01:26:06,605 --> 01:26:09,521
Tayeb(طيِّب) We have rulings regarding Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1090
01:26:10,747 --> 01:26:12,508
What are you distributing over there!!!

1091
01:26:13,421 --> 01:26:15,162
What's going on.?

1092
01:26:15,437 --> 01:26:18,978
keep that stuff until we finish. Keep it until we finish!!!

1093
01:26:20,393 --> 01:26:21,950
No, no food allowed.

1094
01:26:23,170 --> 01:26:23,988
What is that!!!

1095
01:26:26,236 --> 01:26:31,003
If there's time in the end, then we'll have to questions, for now we have to skip the questions.

1096
01:26:32,930 --> 01:26:35,129
Some legal rulings regarding Jihad(جهاد).

1097
01:26:36,740 --> 01:26:40,204
We have rulings regarding Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1098
01:26:41,240 --> 01:26:49,435
After the Ghanimah(غنيمه), booty is gathered, the cost of transport and storing should be taken out from it.

1099
01:26:50,115 --> 01:26:52,782
Then it is split into five equal portions.

1100
01:26:53,314 --> 01:26:56,427
Four out of five is split among the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

1101
01:26:57,060 --> 01:26:59,692
So when we say 4 out of 5, what percentage is that?

1102
01:27:00,811 --> 01:27:01,731
80%!!!

1103
01:27:01,771 --> 01:27:09,589
So 80% goes back to the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), while the 20% left is divided into five portions:

1104
01:27:09,740 --> 01:27:12,041
We are talking about 4% each.

1105
01:27:12,883 --> 01:27:16,443
These 5, 1/5th belongs to Allah and His Messenger.

1106
01:27:16,874 --> 01:27:24,638
This is to be spent on what benefits the Muslims such as building forts or Masajid(مساجد) or any infrastructure for the Ummah(امة).

1107
01:27:25,392 --> 01:27:28,559
1/5th goes to Ahl-Al Bayt(أهل البيت), the household of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1108
01:27:28,853 --> 01:27:33,344
1/5th to the orphans 1/5th to the poor, 1/5th to the Ibn Sabil(إبن سبيل), the wayfarer.

1109
01:27:34,627 --> 01:27:38,668
Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفة) divides the fifth into three and not five.

1110
01:27:39,031 --> 01:27:42,934
So the 20% to Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفة), he is divided into three.

1111
01:27:43,688 --> 01:27:45,229
He excludes the first two,

1112
01:27:45,529 --> 01:27:48,714
He said: 20% goes to the orphans, poor and wayfarer.

1113
01:27:49,188 --> 01:27:53,427
He doesn’t consider the first two of Allah and His Messenger and Ahlul Bait(أهل البيت).

1114
01:27:55,554 --> 01:27:59,573
His opinion is that the portion of Rasool Allah ﷺ and His household ended with his death.

1115
01:28:01,271 --> 01:28:06,602
Imam Malik(إمام مالك) opinion is that the entire 5th should be deposited into the Muslim treasury.

1116
01:28:07,972 --> 01:28:12,619
Not to orphans, it's just taken to the treasury and then the Khalifah(خليفه) spends it as he see fits.

1117
01:28:16,039 --> 01:28:22,609
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says, that the opinion of Malik(مالك) is the opinion of most of the early Muslims and is the most authentic opinion.

1118
01:28:23,044 --> 01:28:28,682
Therefore the opinion of Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) is that 80% goes to the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

1119
01:28:30,357 --> 01:28:32,373
Not all of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), in particular battle.

1120
01:28:33,246 --> 01:28:35,168
And 20% goes to the Treasury.

1121
01:28:37,303 --> 01:28:41,929
And the Imam(اِمَام) spends it as he sees befitting.

1122
01:28:42,866 --> 01:28:49,543
The scholars agree that every Muslim who attends the battle gets his share of booty even if he didn’t fight.

1123
01:28:50,386 --> 01:28:55,764
They also agree that if a person becomes ill in Jihad(جهاد) and cannot fight he still gets his share of booty.

1124
01:28:56,390 --> 01:28:59,149
If a blind or one-legged person attends Jihad(جهاد)

1125
01:28:59,446 --> 01:29:03,632
and they are of benefit to the army they should get their share of booty.

1126
01:29:04,821 --> 01:29:08,158
The 80% of the booty which belong to the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) is divided as follows:

1127
01:29:08,731 --> 01:29:13,514
The horseman get 3 shares, one for himself and two for his horse.

1128
01:29:14,099 --> 01:29:16,172
While the foot soldiers get one share.

1129
01:29:18,441 --> 01:29:24,613
So for example if one share comes out to be 500, pounds.

1130
01:29:26,372 --> 01:29:29,062
The Horseman gets 1500.

1131
01:29:30,484 --> 01:29:35,740
500 for himself and 1000 for his horse, and the foot soldier gets 500.

1132
01:29:37,813 --> 01:29:49,094
So, if we would say that the pilot, and the crew of an armored vehicle or a tank could be counted as horsemen,

1133
01:29:51,762 --> 01:29:56,195
their tank or their aircraft for whatever would get two shares.

1134
01:29:58,886 --> 01:30:04,502
Fix it up, Yani(يعني) for the horse it's to feed it, it's to feed the horse.

1135
01:30:04,994 --> 01:30:08,885
In this situation the fixing of this heavy equipment would be the responsibility of the army

1136
01:30:08,925 --> 01:30:12,117
anyway, it wouldn't be from the that particular share.

1137
01:30:12,640 --> 01:30:18,517
So, these people would get it because of their special skill and training.

1138
01:30:19,087 --> 01:30:22,243
So, they will, they will get more than the foot soldier.

1139
01:30:24,851 --> 01:30:26,048
In the case of Faye(فيئ).

1140
01:30:26,757 --> 01:30:32,392
Now Ghanimah(غنيمه) is what is gained through fighting.

1141
01:30:32,686 --> 01:30:36,094
Faye(فيئ), what is gained without fighting.

1142
01:30:36,332 --> 01:30:43,111
So, an army runs away they leave behind them, some of their belongings that is Faye(فيئ).

1143
01:30:44,159 --> 01:30:46,270
And then there's a third category and that's Salb(سلب).

1144
01:30:46,627 --> 01:30:48,191
Ghanimah(غنيمه), Faye(فيئ) and Salb(سلب).

1145
01:30:48,437 --> 01:30:51,884
Salb(سلب) is what you find on the dead soldier.

1146
01:30:55,784 --> 01:31:00,742
In the case of Faye(فيئ), it belongs in its entirety to the treasury of the Muslims.

1147
01:31:01,564 --> 01:31:07,525
There is a difference of opinion on giving the reinforcement a share of booty if they arrive after the battle is over.

1148
01:31:08,160 --> 01:31:13,884
If there is no Imam(اِمَام) and the Muslims fight the enemy then they split the booty among themselves.

1149
01:31:14,628 --> 01:31:16,417
But if there are women in the booty

1150
01:31:16,552 --> 01:31:22,353
then they are not distributed unless there is an Imam(اِمَام) in order to prevent harmful consequences from happening.

1151
01:31:24,544 --> 01:31:27,171
If someone goes with the intention of fighting

1152
01:31:27,901 --> 01:31:31,085
but they are then relegated to non-fighting positions

1153
01:31:31,411 --> 01:31:36,069
such as guarding the army’s property then such a person gets his share of the booty,

1154
01:31:36,323 --> 01:31:37,760
the cooks, the servants.

1155
01:31:39,561 --> 01:31:44,507
Most scholars state that all of the 80% of the booty must go to the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)

1156
01:31:44,961 --> 01:31:47,379
and no one has authority to divide it otherwise.

1157
01:31:47,762 --> 01:31:50,627
Others do allow the Imam(اِمَام) to give some of it to others.

1158
01:31:51,396 --> 01:31:54,398
If a soldier fails to carry his share and he said:

1159
01:31:54,729 --> 01:31:59,614
Whoever can carry it can take it, then it is allowed for whoever carries it to appropriate it.

1160
01:32:01,265 --> 01:32:04,794
When it comes to property that cannot be transported such as real estate

1161
01:32:05,328 --> 01:32:11,045
then the Imam(اِمَام) has the authority to divide it among the recipients of booty or to make it Waqf(وقف), an endowment.

1162
01:32:11,598 --> 01:32:16,668
Or to give it back to its original owners and charge them Jizya(جِزية) and Kharaaj(خراج) land tax.

1163
01:32:16,977 --> 01:32:22,150
If they become Muslim they are relieved from Jizya(جِزية) but not Kharaaj(خراج).

1164
01:32:24,349 --> 01:32:27,555
In al Hidayah Hanafi(هداية حنفي), which is a Hanafi(حنفي) book.

1165
01:32:27,936 --> 01:32:32,356
If a child fights then he receives a portion of the booty less than one share.

1166
01:32:32,738 --> 01:32:38,171
If a woman participates in nursing and serving then she also receives a portion.

1167
01:32:39,696 --> 01:32:42,783
Nafel(نفل) is an additional reward on top of the share of booty

1168
01:32:42,823 --> 01:32:49,064
that the Imam(اِمَام) can give to the ones, who participate in risky missions or fight exceptionally well.

1169
01:32:49,644 --> 01:32:52,810
That is something more than the share and it is called Nafel(نفل).

1170
01:32:53,604 --> 01:32:56,670
Faye(فيئ) is what is taken from the disbelievers without a fight.

1171
01:32:56,957 --> 01:33:03,134
Such as the disbelievers fearing the Muslims and running away from their positions and they leave behind booty,

1172
01:33:03,529 --> 01:33:07,140
or if they surrender without a fight, or they pay Jizya(جِزية).

1173
01:33:07,505 --> 01:33:10,092
The distribution of the Faye(فيئ) is up to the Imam(اِمَام).

1174
01:33:11,513 --> 01:33:12,670
The prohibition of Ghalool(غلول):

1175
01:33:13,323 --> 01:33:18,666
Ghalool(غلول) is taken away anything from the Ghanimah(غنيمه), before it is split.

1176
01:33:19,545 --> 01:33:25,129
Definition: Ghalool(غلول) is anything worth value a soldier takes from the booty that should be split between the army.

1177
01:33:26,422 --> 01:33:28,212
This does not obviously include Salb(سلب).

1178
01:33:29,288 --> 01:33:35,204
Ghalool(غلول) is Haraam(حرام) no matter how insignificant in value it is and the punishment for it is severe.

1179
01:33:35,859 --> 01:33:36,591
Allah says:

1180
01:33:36,796 --> 01:33:40,381
وَما كانَ لِنَبِيٍّ أَن يَغُلَّ ۚ

1181
01:33:40,643 --> 01:33:45,682
وَمَن يَغلُل يَأتِ بِما غَلَّ يَومَ القِيامَةِ ۚ

1182
01:33:45,953 --> 01:33:52,909
ثُمَّ تُوَفّىٰ كُلُّ نَفسٍ ما كَسَبَت وَهُم لا يُظلَمونَ۞

1183
01:33:53,291 --> 01:33:59,819
It is not attributable to any prophet that he would act unfaithfully, in regard to war booty.

1184
01:34:00,245 --> 01:34:04,131
And whoever takes from it will come with what he took on the Day of Resurrection.

1185
01:34:04,507 --> 01:34:09,825
Then will every soul be compensated for what it earned, and they will not be wronged.

1186
01:34:10,070 --> 01:34:11,467
That’s Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 161.

1187
01:34:11,840 --> 01:34:15,970
Ghalool(غلول) is one of the major sins and there are many Ahadith(احاديث) prohibiting it.

1188
01:34:16,216 --> 01:34:19,378
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: Umar(عُمَر) told me during Khaybar(خَيْبَر)

1189
01:34:20,300 --> 01:34:24,507
some of the Sahabah(صحابه) came saying so and so is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

1190
01:34:25,388 --> 01:34:26,726
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No!

1191
01:34:27,195 --> 01:34:32,716
I’ve seen him in Hellfire because of a piece of cloth which he took from the booty.

1192
01:34:34,242 --> 01:34:35,140
And that’s in Muslim(ألمسلم).

1193
01:34:36,013 --> 01:34:37,188
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated:

1194
01:34:37,672 --> 01:34:43,730
Rasool Allah ﷺ stood one day and spoke to us, he mentioned Ghalool(غلول) and warned us.

1195
01:34:43,825 --> 01:34:49,937
He said: I don’t want to see one of you on the Day of Judgment carrying a camel on his back, saying:

1196
01:34:50,263 --> 01:34:51,826
O Rasool Ullah help me!

1197
01:34:52,183 --> 01:34:53,715
I will say, I cannot help you!

1198
01:34:53,969 --> 01:34:56,018
I have already conveyed a clear message to you.

1199
01:34:56,437 --> 01:35:00,372
I don’t want to see one of you on the Day of Judgment carrying a horse on his back saying:

1200
01:35:00,689 --> 01:35:03,805
O Messenger of Allah help me! I will say: I cannot help you!

1201
01:35:04,022 --> 01:35:05,923
I have already conveyed a clear message to you.

1202
01:35:06,201 --> 01:35:07,008
That’s in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1203
01:35:08,399 --> 01:35:11,424
Abdullah Bin Shaqiq(عبدالله بن شقيق) narrates from a man from Balqeen(بلقين) who said:

1204
01:35:11,907 --> 01:35:15,859
I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he was in Wadi Al Qura(وادي القراء) and he was examining a horse.

1205
01:35:15,899 --> 01:35:19,415
I asked him: O Rasool Ullah, what do you say about the booty?

1206
01:35:19,550 --> 01:35:23,653
He said: To Allah belongs one fifth of it, the rest belongs to the army.

1207
01:35:23,733 --> 01:35:27,624
I said: So no one has a priority in it over someone else?

1208
01:35:27,664 --> 01:35:28,465
He said: No!

1209
01:35:29,481 --> 01:35:35,803
You don’t even have right of ownership over an arrow that you pull out from your own body.

1210
01:35:36,978 --> 01:35:37,837
And that’s in Al-Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي).

1211
01:35:38,647 --> 01:35:41,329
The punishment of Ghalool(غلول) in the Hereafter is that,

1212
01:35:41,409 --> 01:35:45,130
whatever was taken will come on the Day of Judgment and witness against such a person.

1213
01:35:46,781 --> 01:35:50,180
The punishment in this world is that whoever takes anything from the booty,

1214
01:35:50,578 --> 01:35:57,928
would have all of his belongings taken and burnt except what he has taken and that should be returned to the army.

1215
01:35:58,579 --> 01:36:02,702
The opinion of Malik(مالك), As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) and Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفى) is that

1216
01:36:02,742 --> 01:36:05,829
the Ameer(أمير) of the army should punish him as he deems appropriate.

1217
01:36:06,226 --> 01:36:08,704
Imam Abu Bakr Ibn Al Mundir(إمام أبوبكر إبن ألمنذر) says

1218
01:36:08,975 --> 01:36:13,129
that all the scholars agree that the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) are allowed to eat the food of the enemy

1219
01:36:13,412 --> 01:36:17,479
and feed their animals too and it is not Ghalool(غلول) to do so.

1220
01:36:17,978 --> 01:36:18,935
Food is not a problem.

1221
01:36:21,597 --> 01:36:23,102
Rulings regarding Salb(سلب):

1222
01:36:24,903 --> 01:36:33,328
Salb(سلب) is the personnel arms equipments that you find on a dead soldier, it includes everything on the soldier.

1223
01:36:33,935 --> 01:36:39,613
There is a difference of opinion regarding cash, money, whether it is part of Salb(سلب) or part of Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1224
01:36:40,962 --> 01:36:46,801
 Food, ration, ammunition, heavy equipment, that would fall under Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1225
01:36:47,561 --> 01:36:51,906
A land that is opened is Ghanimah(غنيمه), their houses Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1226
01:36:53,379 --> 01:37:01,026
So Salb(سلب) is clear, Salb(سلب) is personnel arms, clothes, cash there is difference of opinion on it.

1227
01:37:01,129 --> 01:37:01,475
Yes!

1228
01:37:01,681 --> 01:37:03,752
Question

1229
01:37:03,895 --> 01:37:06,763
Yes, the soldier you killed personally

1230
01:37:07,394 --> 01:37:09,820
Yeah the modern days it's difficult to tell.

1231
01:37:10,097 --> 01:37:10,900
Question!

1232
01:37:11,820 --> 01:37:14,118
Yes it might fall under Ghanimah(غنيمة)

1233
01:37:14,158 --> 01:37:16,367
But there are situation where people, do know.

1234
01:37:17,375 --> 01:37:18,081
Yani(يعني)

1235
01:37:18,906 --> 01:37:23,322
there is a famous person who, knows where his Kalashionkov came from.

1236
01:37:24,189 --> 01:37:26,220
You remembered where exactly he got it from.

1237
01:37:29,244 --> 01:37:31,417
Some people do know their stuff.

1238
01:37:34,684 --> 01:37:40,949
Some scholars say the fighter takes Salb(سلب) off a soldier he kills with the following conditions:

1239
01:37:42,047 --> 01:37:46,884
N0 1) The killed soldier was fighting with the enemy.

1240
01:37:47,146 --> 01:37:51,064
N0 2) The killed soldier had the ability to defend himself.

1241
01:37:51,185 --> 01:37:55,806
So if he was killed while he was injured or asleep, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) cannot take his Salb(سلب).

1242
01:37:56,930 --> 01:38:02,907
N0 3) If the soldier was withdrawing and was killed from behind then there is no Salb(سلب).

1243
01:38:04,033 --> 01:38:10,544
Other scholars say that the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) takes the Salb(سلب) in every situation he kills an enemy’s soldier,

1244
01:38:10,884 --> 01:38:13,008
whether the soldier was attacking or retreating,

1245
01:38:13,301 --> 01:38:18,806
and their evidence is the previously mentioned Hadith(حديث) of the story of Abu Salamah(أبوسلمة) to support this view.

1246
01:38:19,270 --> 01:38:20,159
They were running away.

1247
01:38:23,802 --> 01:38:30,156
Is it necessary for the Imam(اِمَام) to state that whoever kills an enemy soldier gets his Salb(سلب)

1248
01:38:30,236 --> 01:38:31,936
or his Salb(سلب) taken by default?

1249
01:38:33,245 --> 01:38:39,692
As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) and Ahmad(أحمد) say the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) gets the Salb(سلب) whether the Imam(اِمَام) states that or not.

1250
01:38:40,414 --> 01:38:41,851
Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفة) states that

1251
01:38:41,891 --> 01:38:47,331
if the Imam(اِمَام) does not state that the Salb(سلب) goes to the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) who kills the enemy then it falls under Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1252
01:38:50,132 --> 01:38:55,135
Al-Awza’e(ألأوزاعي) states that the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) can take all the Salb(سلب) of the killed enemy soldier

1253
01:38:55,508 --> 01:38:58,040
even his clothes and leave him naked.

1254
01:38:59,206 --> 01:39:01,121
This is also the opinion of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

1255
01:39:01,756 --> 01:39:06,253
Al-Thawri(ألثوري) and Ibn Mundhir(إبن منذر) discourage that because it exposes the Awrah(عورة).

1256
01:39:10,508 --> 01:39:12,699
I mean who would want his clothes, anyway.

1257
01:39:13,760 --> 01:39:15,782
In those days Yani(يعني) clothes had value.

1258
01:39:19,641 --> 01:39:22,527
Rulings regarding Muslim POWs:

1259
01:39:23,590 --> 01:39:27,750
If a Muslim POW is able to escape then it is mandatory on him to do so.

1260
01:39:28,401 --> 01:39:34,355
If he can escape and capture with him any enemy, take any of their property, or kill among them then he should.

1261
01:39:35,171 --> 01:39:41,456
If the POW is released with conditions that he agrees to, then he must fulfill those conditions

1262
01:39:42,059 --> 01:39:47,725
in order not to end up harming other Muslim POWs or causing the enemy to think that the Muslims are untrustworthy.

1263
01:39:49,523 --> 01:39:55,453
The Muslim POW is not allowed to marry a Christian or a Jew in the land of disbelief

1264
01:39:55,952 --> 01:39:59,717
because the children in this case might follow their mother’s religion.

1265
01:40:00,254 --> 01:40:07,949
By the way, I've heard that Al-Qazavi(ألقضاوي) has given a similar fatwa(فتوى) regarding Muslims in the West.

1266
01:40:08,443 --> 01:40:12,861
He said that they should not marry Christian women or Jewish women, because of this issue,

1267
01:40:13,845 --> 01:40:16,817
that you don't know what religion, the kids will grow into.

1268
01:40:18,155 --> 01:40:19,369
So he considers it to be Haram(حرام).

1269
01:40:19,964 --> 01:40:21,885
And he is not allowed to marry a Muslim

1270
01:40:22,485 --> 01:40:28,844
because they could force them and their children to apostasy or they could be enslaved.

1271
01:40:30,146 --> 01:40:33,866
The Muslim POW should be patient until they return to Muslim land.

1272
01:40:35,767 --> 01:40:38,239
Rulings regarding the enemy POWs:

1273
01:40:39,831 --> 01:40:44,237
The stronger opinion is that the Imam(اِمَام) should do what is most beneficial for the Muslims.

1274
01:40:44,646 --> 01:40:48,214
To execute them, to free them without anything in return,

1275
01:40:48,681 --> 01:40:54,758
to free them in return of freeing Muslim POWs, to charge for their freedom, or to enslave them.

1276
01:40:55,826 --> 01:41:00,152
The ruling on women and children POWs is that they become slaves by default.

1277
01:41:01,239 --> 01:41:05,786
If a Muslim kills a POW, the Ameer(أمير) has the right to punish him by Ta'zeer(تعزير),

1278
01:41:06,444 --> 01:41:10,548
which is a punishment less than the least punishment of a major sin, it's usually 10 lashes.

1279
01:41:11,825 --> 01:41:18,169
If a man is taken as a POW along with his wife some scholars say that the marriage contract becomes null

1280
01:41:18,693 --> 01:41:22,837
while others say it remains.

1281
01:41:23,503 --> 01:41:27,235
The same is said when the husband alone falls into captivity.

1282
01:41:27,718 --> 01:41:33,556
But if a woman is taken as a POW then if she is married her marriage contract is nullified,

1283
01:41:34,493 --> 01:41:38,138
the marriage is over and she would be taken by somebody else.

1284
01:41:38,877 --> 01:41:43,894
Question

1285
01:41:44,846 --> 01:41:46,410
There's a difference of opinion on these two.

1286
01:41:46,952 --> 01:41:51,571
Are you talking about alone or if a man and women are taken together,

1287
01:41:52,221 --> 01:41:55,281
there's a difference of opinion whether the marriage is nullified or not.

1288
01:41:55,869 --> 01:42:04,761
However, if a man is taken separately and a woman is taken separately, then their respective marriages are nullified.

1289
01:42:05,415 --> 01:42:12,706
Question

1290
01:42:13,172 --> 01:42:18,381
I think our schlolars never even dreamed of us situations.

1291
01:42:20,097 --> 01:42:26,925
When children fall into captivity with their parents are they considered Muslim or non-Muslim?

1292
01:42:27,884 --> 01:42:32,396
The opinion of As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي), Ahmad(أحمد), Malik(مالك), and Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفة), which is the four.

1293
01:42:33,139 --> 01:42:38,313
Is that they follow the religion of their parents and are considered non-Muslim.

1294
01:42:39,287 --> 01:42:43,429
If captured with the father then Ahmad(أحمد) considers them to be Muslim,

1295
01:42:43,580 --> 01:42:46,316
while the other three Imam(اِمَام)s state that they are not.

1296
01:42:47,000 --> 01:42:51,291
If the children are captured with their mother then according to Ahmad(أحمد) they are Muslim.

1297
01:42:51,962 --> 01:42:54,242
As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) and Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفة) say they are not.

1298
01:42:54,928 --> 01:43:00,588
If the children are captured alone then according to all the Imam(اِمَام)s except As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي), they are Muslim.

1299
01:43:01,407 --> 01:43:05,708
According to the majority opinion the captured families should not be separated.

1300
01:43:06,718 --> 01:43:07,914
Miscellaneous issues:

1301
01:43:08,847 --> 01:43:16,457
Offensive Jihad(جهاد) without the permission of the Imam(اِمَام) or whoever represents him is Makrooh(مكروع) but it is not Haram(حرام).

1302
01:43:17,330 --> 01:43:20,551
There are exceptions to the discouragement:

1303
01:43:21,157 --> 01:43:25,567
N0 1) If Jihad(جهاد) is urgent and does not accept delay

1304
01:43:25,964 --> 01:43:29,868
and seeking permission would delay it, then permission of the Imam(اِمَام) is not needed.

1305
01:43:31,440 --> 01:43:38,362
N0 2). If the Imam(اِمَام) neglects Jihad(جهاد) and he and his soldiers are attached to this world.

1306
01:43:38,917 --> 01:43:44,170
In this case the permission of the Imam(اِمَام) is not to be sought because the Imam(اِمَام) has suspended Jihad(جهاد).

1307
01:43:44,726 --> 01:43:48,468
The Mujahideen(مجاهدين) should therefore resume it, and this is the case we have now.

1308
01:43:49,629 --> 01:43:52,390
N0 3) If the person cannot seek permission

1309
01:43:52,705 --> 01:43:57,602
because he knows in advance that the Imam(اِمَام) would not give him permission, which is also, what we have now.

1310
01:43:58,434 --> 01:44:05,133
N0 4) Ibn Qudama(إبن قدامة) states that: The absence of the Imam(اِمَام) should not be a reason for the delay of Jihad(جهاد).

1311
01:44:05,540 --> 01:44:13,088
And this would also be the view among the ones who hold that the leaders now are Murtaddeen(مُرتَدين),

1312
01:44:13,904 --> 01:44:15,215
therefore they are not even Imam(اِمَام),

1313
01:44:15,590 --> 01:44:20,865
so you would apply what Ibn Qudama(إبن قدامة) said, in the absence of an Imam(اِمَام), you fight without an Imam(اِمَام).

1314
01:44:21,969 --> 01:44:24,249
 It is Sunnah(سنة) for the Ameer(أمير), commander of the army

1315
01:44:24,289 --> 01:44:28,260
to take a pledge from the soldiers not to turn their backs in battle

1316
01:44:28,700 --> 01:44:34,291
as the Messenger of Allahﷺ did in Hudaybiyah(حديبية), he took their pledge.

1317
01:44:34,738 --> 01:44:36,856
It is also Sunnah(سنة) for the Ameer(أمير) to:

1318
01:44:37,046 --> 01:44:42,857
N0 1) Send reconnaissance missions and to gather information about the enemy.

1319
01:44:43,076 --> 01:44:46,647
N0 2) Set out on Thursday morning if that is possible.

1320
01:44:47,173 --> 01:44:51,603
N0 3) Divide the army into brigades under separate banners

1321
01:44:51,898 --> 01:45:02,857
and to have each brigade have its own distinguishing insignia, a motto or a sign or envelope, for each section of the army.

1322
01:45:04,077 --> 01:45:11,477
N0 4) To employ each and every method that would terrorize the enemy.

1323
01:45:13,988 --> 01:45:20,485
N0 5) Seek assistance from the weak, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You are given victory through the weak among you.

1324
01:45:20,954 --> 01:45:23,313
N0 6) Make Dua(دُعَا) when the armies meet.

1325
01:45:23,710 --> 01:45:27,547
N0 7) Encourage the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) to fight and be steadfast.

1326
01:45:28,280 --> 01:45:33,670
N0 8) Make takbeer(تكبير) along with the army without extravagance in raising voice.

1327
01:45:34,096 --> 01:45:42,974
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِذا لَقيتُم فِئَةً فَاثبُتوا

1328
01:45:43,414 --> 01:45:48,836
وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ۞

1329
01:45:50,016 --> 01:45:54,798
O you who have believed, when you encounter a company from the enemy forces stand firm

1330
01:45:54,884 --> 01:45:57,384
and remember Allah that you may be successful.

1331
01:45:57,424 --> 01:46:00,913
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِذا لَقيتُم فِئَةً فَاثبُتوا وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ۞

1332
01:46:05,417 --> 01:46:06,736
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says:

1333
01:46:10,567 --> 01:46:15,903
The remembrance should be done silently because raising voices with zikr(زكر) in battle is discouraged,

1334
01:46:16,458 --> 01:46:24,503
if it is one person but if it is by a group then it is acceptable if it weakens the morale of the enemy.

1335
01:46:25,130 --> 01:46:28,289
The companions used to dislike raising voices in battle.

1336
01:46:31,624 --> 01:46:38,086
It is mandatory to convey the message of Islam to whoever did not hear it and this should be done before fighting.

1337
01:46:38,406 --> 01:46:44,616
But if they did hear about Islam before, then calling them to Islam again is not necessary before fighting them

1338
01:46:45,018 --> 01:46:50,434
 but it is good to do since they might become Muslim this time.

1339
01:46:51,574 --> 01:46:57,932
It appears from Sunnah(سنة) that giving Da'wah(دعوة) prior to fighting is not necessary with special operation groups,

1340
01:46:58,444 --> 01:47:01,971
 which are groups of Mujahideen(مجاهدين) sent for a specific mission

1341
01:47:02,245 --> 01:47:05,723
such as the group sent to assassinate Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) for example.

1342
01:47:06,057 --> 01:47:11,957
This is important ruling today, the issue of Aqamat-Ul-Hujah(إقامة الحجة), has Da'wah(دعوة) been delivered or not.

1343
01:47:13,350 --> 01:47:15,716
And what is considered to be delivering of the Da'wah(دعوة),

1344
01:47:16,178 --> 01:47:23,194
in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the delivering of the Da'wah(دعوة) wouldn't teach them everything about Islam,

1345
01:47:23,793 --> 01:47:28,425
and try to convince them with every single method in the toolbox.

1346
01:47:29,088 --> 01:47:32,135
It would be a brief letter of two or three lines become Muslim.

1347
01:47:35,040 --> 01:47:38,828
If you do this, what will happen, if you don't, this is what would happen, and that was it.

1348
01:47:38,972 --> 01:47:45,954
That was considered to be the Da'wah(دعوة) that is delivered to these disbelievers,

1349
01:47:47,090 --> 01:47:48,783
and they haven't heard anything about Islam

1350
01:47:48,823 --> 01:47:51,374
because they didn't have mass media in those days

1351
01:47:51,454 --> 01:47:58,375
to teach them anything about Islam, people were living in their own settlements in the desert separated and secluded.

1352
01:47:59,773 --> 01:48:02,672
 And when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص)

1353
01:48:02,712 --> 01:48:07,113
and Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح) went into the land of the Romans and the Persians,

1354
01:48:07,481 --> 01:48:12,809
they didn't know much about Islam and their letters were very brief, and we read, some of their letters.

1355
01:48:13,703 --> 01:48:17,343
So, to say now that the world has not heard about Islam is not true.

1356
01:48:18,169 --> 01:48:24,424
They have heard a lot more than the recipients of the letters of  Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1357
01:48:25,716 --> 01:48:26,498
A lot more!

1358
01:48:27,466 --> 01:48:34,763
Overall, the entire population of Earth today must have heard the name Islam,

1359
01:48:35,006 --> 01:48:40,817
must have heard the name of Muhammadﷺ, and must know something about Islam, Salah(صلاة), Hajj(حَجْ).

1360
01:48:42,852 --> 01:48:45,835
And that is a sufficient form of Da'wah(دعوة).

1361
01:48:45,875 --> 01:48:56,933
I mean, because sometimes we say that no, the thing is that they have heard stereotypes about Islam, they've heard the wrong message.

1362
01:48:57,862 --> 01:48:59,782
They have not been taught the truth about Islam.

1363
01:48:59,822 --> 01:49:02,121
Well that was the same in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1364
01:49:02,386 --> 01:49:09,061
All what they heard that Muhammadﷺ is insane, a magician, a sorcerer, a fortune teller, a liar,

1365
01:49:09,101 --> 01:49:10,616
that's what they heard about Muhammadﷺ

1366
01:49:11,101 --> 01:49:15,040
and Sahabah(صحابه) didn't go arguing with them proving to them otherwise, they just told them become Muslim.

1367
01:49:17,227 --> 01:49:24,534
So, CNN has done the job, BBC has done the job, spreading the Da'wah(دعوة), they've all done it.

1368
01:49:27,107 --> 01:49:30,736
They've talked about Islam and they've raised the issue to the forefront

1369
01:49:30,776 --> 01:49:35,628
so that's what people talk about today, over their dinner table.

1370
01:49:36,359 --> 01:49:38,860
Talk about Islam, talk about the Muslims.

1371
01:49:39,660 --> 01:49:43,965
There was a time I could remember when you would be listening to the news.

1372
01:49:45,806 --> 01:49:48,424
You would hear nothing about Islam or Muslims, at all!

1373
01:49:50,448 --> 01:50:00,856
And Islam was this exotic foreign thing that goes back, it's a historical thing, it doesn't even relate to the real world today.

1374
01:50:02,055 --> 01:50:05,031
And slowly but surely Islam started coming to the forefront.

1375
01:50:05,111 --> 01:50:15,245
Now, it is impossible to have a news broadcast, that is not talking about Islam or Muslims, for at least half of the time.

1376
01:50:17,441 --> 01:50:19,482
 There is either going to be news coming from Iraq,

1377
01:50:19,932 --> 01:50:24,267
or from Saudia(سعودية) or from Afghanistan, or from Shishan(شيشان), or from Kashmir,

1378
01:50:24,844 --> 01:50:29,863
there's gonna be something about Islam or Muslims on the news, day in and day out.

1379
01:50:31,348 --> 01:50:34,736
So the Muslims and Islam are the focus of attention today.

1380
01:50:36,085 --> 01:50:44,708
And the events of history are revolving around this Ummah(امة) because this Ummah(امة) is representative of Al-Haqq(حَقّ).

1381
01:50:47,477 --> 01:50:51,983
Jizya(جِزية) is accepted from the Jews and Christians, if they pay it they are allowed to practice their religion.

1382
01:50:52,023 --> 01:50:54,954
Jizya(جِزية) is also accepted from those who are similar to the people of the book

1383
01:50:55,310 --> 01:50:58,757
and might have received a book from Allah such as the Zoroastrians

1384
01:50:59,645 --> 01:51:02,693
because of Shuba-Tur-Risala(شبهة الرسالة), the scholar said about Shuba-Tur-Risala(شبهة الرسالة).

1385
01:51:03,788 --> 01:51:08,974
So if this applies to Zoroastrians, it could also apply to the Buddhists,

1386
01:51:09,085 --> 01:51:13,635
however, it cannot apply to Hindus because this is clear, pagan worshipping,

1387
01:51:13,940 --> 01:51:22,562
it cannot apply to any form of religion that is paganistic in it's nature.

1388
01:51:23,371 --> 01:51:24,371
Question

1389
01:51:25,110 --> 01:51:26,165
It is a safe(سيف), sword.

1390
01:51:26,823 --> 01:51:30,018
The option is Islam or the sword.

1391
01:51:31,069 --> 01:51:39,897
Islam gives an exception to the Christians and the Jews because they have a trace of truth in their religion.

1392
01:51:40,915 --> 01:51:49,867
And because of this truth, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is giving them the benefit of the doubt and giving them time to study and think about Islam,

1393
01:51:51,206 --> 01:51:56,996
because they believe in the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), even though they believe in an a wrong understanding of prophet hood.

1394
01:51:58,041 --> 01:52:02,524
 They believe in Allah but they have a wrong understanding of the Asma o Sifat(أسماءالصفات) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1395
01:52:03,159 --> 01:52:10,993
But because of that trace of truth in there, which is used by Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) to convince them to buy the rest which is false.

1396
01:52:11,795 --> 01:52:13,875
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is giving them a chance.

1397
01:52:14,303 --> 01:52:17,116
However, when it comes to pagan worshipping.

1398
01:52:17,902 --> 01:52:26,922
If a human being descends to shut such a low level of worshipping a rock or an animal, then such a person does not deserve to live anymore.

1399
01:52:27,575 --> 01:52:34,898
Islam does not give them the right to live anymore because they have pulled themselves down to the lowest levels.

1400
01:52:35,914 --> 01:52:39,430
And that is against the Takrim(تكريم) that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has given to the Son of Adam(آدَم).

1401
01:52:39,470 --> 01:52:40,311
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

1402
01:52:40,541 --> 01:52:51,628
وَلَقَد كَرَّمنا بَني آدَمَ وَحَمَلناهُم فِي البَرِّ وَالبَحرِ وَرَزَقناهُم مِنَ الطَّيِّباتِ

1403
01:52:52,493 --> 01:53:03,984
وَرَزَقناهُم مِنَ الطَّيِّباتِ وَفَضَّلناهُم عَلىٰ كَثيرٍ مِمَّن خَلَقنا تَفضيلًا۞

1404
01:53:04,446 --> 01:53:05,818
وَلَقَد كَرَّمنا بَني آدَمَ

1405
01:53:06,675 --> 01:53:08,686
We have honored the son of Adam(آدَم),

1406
01:53:09,025 --> 01:53:11,477
so they have rejected that honor which Allah gave them,

1407
01:53:11,858 --> 01:53:17,306
and they have put themselves in a low level of worship in rock or an animal.

1408
01:53:17,655 --> 01:53:20,506
Therefore Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not give them the right to exist anymore.

1409
01:53:21,171 --> 01:53:24,138
So the option is either to become Muslim, or the sword.

1410
01:53:26,429 --> 01:53:30,905
The time will be up for the Christians and the Jews when Eesa(عيسى) comes, the chance is over.

1411
01:53:30,945 --> 01:53:41,019
You would have had centuries and centuries to sit on it, give it a second thought, if that wasn't enough.

1412
01:53:42,360 --> 01:53:44,707
This is the deadline, there's no more Jizya(جِزية) anymore.

1413
01:53:45,850 --> 01:53:50,752
If the enemy attacks Muslim land and the Muslims did not fight them,

1414
01:53:51,728 --> 01:53:56,742
then their neglect of Jihad(جهاد) is the same as turning one’s back in the battlefield,

1415
01:53:56,903 --> 01:53:58,235
this is a very important Hukum(حكم).

1416
01:54:01,267 --> 01:54:06,228
So this would apply to the Falastine(فلسطين), to Iraq, to Shishan(شيشان), to Kashmir, the ones who are living there,

1417
01:54:08,039 --> 01:54:16,813
 and they decide not to resist and fight, they have committed the sin of retreat in the battlefield,

1418
01:54:17,592 --> 01:54:20,442
unless there's an excuse for not being able to fight.

1419
01:54:21,505 --> 01:54:25,685
This is if the Muslims are more than half the number of the their enemy.

1420
01:54:26,051 --> 01:54:30,937
But if they are too few to fight than they can fortify themselves and wait for reinforcements.

1421
01:54:31,916 --> 01:54:36,539
If the Imam(اِمَام) invites the Muslims to Jihad(جهاد) that is originally classified as Fardh Kifayah(فرض كفاية),

1422
01:54:36,973 --> 01:54:41,637
it becomes a Fardh Ain(فرض عين) on each one of them because it is mandatory to obey the Imam(اِمَام).

1423
01:54:42,004 --> 01:54:45,370
The oppression of an Imam(اِمَام) should not prevent from Jihad(جهاد) with him.

1424
01:54:46,500 --> 01:54:50,770
It is acceptable to fight with an Imam(اِمَام) who drinks or commits major sins

1425
01:54:51,064 --> 01:54:54,601
because these sins affect him but Jihad(جهاد) benefits everyone.

1426
01:54:54,999 --> 01:55:01,786
So Jihad(جهاد) is so important, you are even order to fight under it, a leader who drinks.

1427
01:55:03,303 --> 01:55:04,848
So Jihad(جهاد) should never stop.

1428
01:55:06,102 --> 01:55:09,523
It is not allowed to kill women and children if they don’t fight

1429
01:55:09,563 --> 01:55:13,689
but if they do fight then there is no doubt that it is allowed to kill them.

1430
01:55:14,103 --> 01:55:19,325
It is also the consensus of scholars that if an old man fights then it is allowed to kill him.

1431
01:55:19,840 --> 01:55:22,578
That also applies to the weak, blind, and handicapped.

1432
01:55:23,014 --> 01:55:28,932
The ruling also applies if any of the above aided in fighting the Muslims with their intellect..

1433
01:55:29,563 --> 01:55:38,906
So, one might argue here for fighting the ones who pay taxes to a government that fights against the Muslims.

1434
01:55:39,815 --> 01:55:47,398
The opinion of the vast majority of scholars is that monks and anyone devoted to worship in monasteries are not to be killed.

1435
01:55:47,909 --> 01:55:50,554
The opinion of the majority of scholars is that merchants,

1436
01:55:51,362 --> 01:55:57,673
skilled workers and employees should not be killed if they are not involved in fighting Muslims.

1437
01:55:58,416 --> 01:56:02,410
It is allowed to fire catapults on the disbelievers and to flood them with water

1438
01:56:02,781 --> 01:56:06,593
even if that would lead to the death of Muslim POWs in their hands

1439
01:56:06,892 --> 01:56:10,401
since this is a necessity of war, let alone women and children.

1440
01:56:12,036 --> 01:56:14,652
If the enemy uses Muslim human shields:

1441
01:56:15,242 --> 01:56:20,427
If it is not necessary to strike the disbelievers than they are left in order to protect the Muslims.

1442
01:56:21,465 --> 01:56:26,620
If there is a need to strike at the disbelievers such as if there is a battle going on,

1443
01:56:27,250 --> 01:56:31,425
or if we leave them alone they would gain victory over Muslims,

1444
01:56:31,709 --> 01:56:38,539
then they should be attacked even if that would lead to the loss of life among the Muslim human shields.

1445
01:56:40,501 --> 01:56:45,843
It is allowed to ambush an enemy at night even if there are women and children among them

1446
01:56:46,121 --> 01:56:48,523
since that is a necessity of Jihad(جهاد).

1447
01:56:49,899 --> 01:56:55,142
The ruling regarding trees and plants in the land of the disbelievers falls into three categories:

1448
01:56:55,245 --> 01:56:59,866
Number 1). Trees that the Muslims need to cut down:

1449
01:57:00,509 --> 01:57:03,027
In such case it is allowed to cut down.

1450
01:57:03,397 --> 01:57:06,641
Such as when these trees are close to the fortresses of the disbelievers

1451
01:57:06,958 --> 01:57:11,031
or when trees get in their way or prevents them from widening their roads

1452
01:57:11,291 --> 01:57:14,662
or if the disbelievers are cutting down the trees in the Muslim lands.

1453
01:57:15,356 --> 01:57:19,013
Number 2) Trees that if cut down would harm the Muslims:

1454
01:57:19,301 --> 01:57:24,690
Such as trees needed for their cattle, in such a case it is illegal to cut them down.

1455
01:57:24,730 --> 01:57:28,881
Number 3) Trees that if cut down won't cause any harm to the Muslims:

1456
01:57:29,333 --> 01:57:33,982
If cutting them down would harm the disbelievers or anger them then they could be cut down.

1457
01:57:37,956 --> 01:57:43,514
The Muslim who discourages others from fighting should be banned from joining any army of Jihad(جهاد).

1458
01:57:44,165 --> 01:57:47,852
If he did go out then he should not receive any portion of the booty

1459
01:57:48,217 --> 01:57:53,452
or any due compensation as a punishment for his discouragement of Jihad(جهاد).

1460
01:57:54,511 --> 01:57:57,297
The discourager is the one who would say for example:

1461
01:57:57,741 --> 01:58:03,759
The enemy is too strong or our horses are weak or we cannot defeat them.

1462
01:58:04,342 --> 01:58:07,590
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) quite a lot of muslims, to say that today.

1463
01:58:08,612 --> 01:58:11,604
Or such statements that imply that we should not fight.

1464
01:58:12,409 --> 01:58:16,291
Close to that, if the person who spreads rumors that weaken the Muslims.

1465
01:58:17,829 --> 01:58:20,825
It is allowed for the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) to take from Zaka'at(زكوة) even if he is wealthy.

1466
01:58:21,776 --> 01:58:28,185
He can only take money for his necessities of food, clothing, travel expenses, and to purchase needed arms.

1467
01:58:28,519 --> 01:58:30,900
He can also give his family from this money.

1468
01:58:31,829 --> 01:58:32,718
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says

1469
01:58:32,758 --> 01:58:36,713
that Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) in the Ayah(آية) of Zaka'at(زكوة) refers to the ones in Jihad(جهاد) and Ribat(رباط).

1470
01:58:38,157 --> 01:58:43,975
If the enemy is more than double the size of the Muslim army then the Muslims are allowed to withdraw, if not then they must fight.

1471
01:58:45,148 --> 01:58:49,339
The scholars have three views on seeking assistance from non-Muslims in combat:

1472
01:58:49,537 --> 01:58:56,821
Number 1) It is allowed, if the Muslims take precautions from any possible betrayal from the non-Muslim side.

1473
01:58:57,914 --> 01:59:02,769
Number 2) It is allowed to have them only in lowly roles such as service.

1474
01:59:03,156 --> 01:59:05,224
Number 3) It is not allowed at all.

1475
01:59:07,203 --> 01:59:13,044
If a nonbeliever embraces Islam then his blood and wealth are protected

1476
01:59:13,493 --> 01:59:17,802
whether he became a Muslim in the state of piece or the state of war.

1477
01:59:18,590 --> 01:59:20,373
This is the consensus of scholars.

1478
01:59:21,026 --> 01:59:25,830
But if he becomes Muslim after falling into captivity, what happens then?

1479
01:59:26,028 --> 01:59:31,820
So what happens if you have this prisoner of war, and he becomes a Muslim?

1480
01:59:36,205 --> 01:59:37,205
and then

1481
01:59:43,670 --> 01:59:45,104
What happens?

1482
01:59:46,826 --> 01:59:50,454
But if he becomes Muslim after falling into captivity,

1483
01:59:51,740 --> 01:59:57,416
then his blood is protected and the Imam(اِمَام) then has the choices of enslaving him or freeing him.

1484
01:59:58,510 --> 02:00:04,236
However Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) says that the Imam(اِمَام) does not have the option but to enslave such a person.

1485
02:00:05,665 --> 02:00:07,746
So his life is spared, he is not killed.

1486
02:00:08,579 --> 02:00:14,023
However, he is enslaved, according to Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), according to other Imam(اِمَام)s he can be freed.

1487
02:00:15,222 --> 02:00:19,604
If enemy soldiers lose their way and end up in a Muslim town,

1488
02:00:19,952 --> 02:00:24,456
they and their belongings become Faye(فيئ) for the Muslims of that town.

1489
02:00:26,647 --> 02:00:32,876
If enemy soldiers enter the land of Islam without an agreement then it is allowed to kill them and take their property.

1490
02:00:34,153 --> 02:00:39,875
 Or if they enter with an agreement that is signed by a Murtadd(مُرتَد), government.

1491
02:00:42,042 --> 02:00:50,994
I asked some of the great scholars of the As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) schools about the businessmen who are from the land of the enemy

1492
02:00:51,412 --> 02:00:57,730
and come to do business in Muslim land, is it allowed to fight them at sea before they reach our ports?

1493
02:00:57,856 --> 02:01:02,212
In other words, before they get into our lands because the Ahad(عهد) implies then.

1494
02:01:03,388 --> 02:01:08,289
They said: They can be fought before they get to our ports and even after they get to our ports.

1495
02:01:09,773 --> 02:01:14,116
If enemy businessmen enter Muslim territory by permission to do business

1496
02:01:14,656 --> 02:01:17,645
then the Muslims should not transgress against them.

1497
02:01:19,052 --> 02:01:22,952
If a Dhimmi(ضِمِّي), a Christian or Jew living in Muslim territory who pays Jizya(جِزية)

1498
02:01:23,346 --> 02:01:29,030
wants to join the enemy in their fight against Muslims he should be prevented from doing so.

1499
02:01:30,504 --> 02:01:36,949
There is a difference of opinion on beheading the disbelievers and then transporting their heads to a different location.

1500
02:01:39,997 --> 02:01:44,139
Some consider it to be illegal because this is an act of mutilation

1501
02:01:44,715 --> 02:01:48,012
and is imitating the disbelievers since these are their actions.

1502
02:01:48,827 --> 02:01:50,571
Other scholars say that it is allowed

1503
02:01:51,179 --> 02:01:55,234
and they cite the incident when the head of Rifa'ah Bin Qais(رفاع بن قيس) was presented to Rasool Ullah

1504
02:01:55,726 --> 02:02:01,025
and when Fayrooz Ad- Daylami(فيروزالديلمي) brought Rasool Allah ﷺ the head of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسودألأنسي) who claimed prophet hood.

1505
02:02:02,567 --> 02:02:05,096
Can a Muslim grant protection to a disbeliever?

1506
02:02:06,571 --> 02:02:11,936
The majority of the scholars say a Muslim can grant a disbeliever or a small number of them, protection

1507
02:02:12,214 --> 02:02:13,910
and the Muslims should honor that.

1508
02:02:14,944 --> 02:02:18,383
The spy cannot be given protection and must be killed.

1509
02:02:19,659 --> 02:02:24,740
If a disbeliever who was already granted protection turns out to be a spy then he should be killed.

1510
02:02:26,518 --> 02:02:34,315
If the Muslim is weak in the land of disbelievers and is not able to publicly show his religion then it is Haram(حرام) to live there.

1511
02:02:35,159 --> 02:02:37,519
If he is unable to emigrate then he is excused.

1512
02:02:38,080 --> 02:02:41,381
If the Muslim is strong and able to publicly practice Islam

1513
02:02:41,904 --> 02:02:47,026
than they can live in the disbelievers land but it is still recommended to move to a Muslim land.

1514
02:02:50,280 --> 02:02:54,991
Scholars consider that a Muslims should not travel to the land of the disbelievers for business

1515
02:02:55,547 --> 02:02:59,041
and they consider the one who does that to be a fasiq(فاسق).

1516
02:03:00,787 --> 02:03:04,923
It is also Haram(حرام) to sell the disbelievers weapons and whoever does that should be punished.

1517
02:03:06,310 --> 02:03:10,246
Scholars say that Muslim women should never be taken to the land of the enemy

1518
02:03:10,619 --> 02:03:13,897
unless they are within a large Muslim army to protect them.

1519
02:03:14,431 --> 02:03:18,846
They also say that Muslim women should not settle in the dangerous borderlands of the Muslims,

1520
02:03:19,161 --> 02:03:24,062
so you can see that the issue of honor, and the protection of the Muslim women is paramount to Muslims.

1521
02:03:26,496 --> 02:03:27,724
The Last Chapter!

1522
02:03:29,321 --> 02:03:31,644
Ready! Are you tired?

1523
02:03:33,588 --> 02:03:37,155
It's not long it's not long.

1524
02:03:38,880 --> 02:03:41,591
CHAPTER 17: A BRIEF CHAPTER ON THE ART OF WAR:

1525
02:03:42,248 --> 02:03:47,589
Allah mentions five things, if they exist in a fighting group,

1526
02:03:48,058 --> 02:03:51,736
(By the way this is the last chapter in the book we're finishing the book, Al-hamdolillah)

1527
02:03:53,750 --> 02:04:02,879
Allah mentions five things, if they exist in a fighting group, they would definitely win regardless of their numbers.

1528
02:04:04,066 --> 02:04:07,932
These five attributes are mentioned in the following two verses:

1529
02:04:08,463 --> 02:04:17,436
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِذا لَقيتُم فِئَةً فَاثبُتوا

1530
02:04:17,814 --> 02:04:23,136
وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ۞

1531
02:04:23,654 --> 02:04:31,396
 وَأَطيعُوا اللَّهَ وَرَسولَهُ وَلا تَنازَعوا فَتَفشَلوا وَتَذهَبَ ريحُكُم ۖ

1532
02:04:31,776 --> 02:04:37,320
وَاصبِروا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ۞

1533
02:04:38,153 --> 02:04:45,499
O you who have believed, when you encounter a company from the enemy forces, stand firm

1534
02:04:45,678 --> 02:04:46,558
(فَاثبُتوا)

1535
02:04:48,647 --> 02:04:49,674
and remember Allah

1536
02:04:49,824 --> 02:04:53,697
(وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ).

1537
02:04:53,760 --> 02:04:56,590
And remember Allah much that you may be successful.

1538
02:04:56,971 --> 02:04:58,661
And obey Allah and His Messenger

1539
02:04:58,987 --> 02:05:00,177
(وَأَطيعُوا اللَّهَ وَرَسولَهُ).

1540
02:05:00,463 --> 02:05:03,109
And do not dispute and thus lose courage

1541
02:05:03,871 --> 02:05:05,784
and then your strength would depart

1542
02:05:06,379 --> 02:05:08,698
(وَلا تَنازَعوا فَتَفشَلوا وَتَذهَبَ ريحُكُم ۖ وَاصبِروا)

1543
02:05:09,157 --> 02:05:12,130
and be patient. Indeed Allah is with the patient

1544
02:05:12,249 --> 02:05:13,352
(إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ).

1545
02:05:13,670 --> 02:05:14,797
So what are the five?

1546
02:05:15,439 --> 02:05:17,401
Number 1) Being steadfast .

1547
02:05:18,360 --> 02:05:19,051
(فَاثبُتوا)

1548
02:05:19,440 --> 02:05:20,122
Number 2)

1549
02:05:20,447 --> 02:05:21,946
وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا

1550
02:05:22,241 --> 02:05:23,446
The Remembrance of Allah.

1551
02:05:23,771 --> 02:05:24,586
Number3)

1552
02:05:24,745 --> 02:05:26,348
وَأَطيعُوا اللَّهَ وَرَسولَهُ

1553
02:05:26,634 --> 02:05:28,207
Obey Allah and His Messenger.

1554
02:05:28,524 --> 02:05:29,389
Number 4 )

1555
02:05:29,778 --> 02:05:30,778
وَلا تَنازَعوا

1556
02:05:30,905 --> 02:05:32,464
Avoid disputes.

1557
02:05:33,115 --> 02:05:34,187
And Number 5)

1558
02:05:34,274 --> 02:05:34,980
Patience

1559
02:05:35,210 --> 02:05:36,242
(وَاصبِروا)

1560
02:05:37,389 --> 02:05:40,900
These five if you fulfill them, if you stick to them, you never lose.

1561
02:05:41,959 --> 02:05:43,078
They should be memorized.

1562
02:05:43,801 --> 02:05:44,961
What are they, Again! Number 1)

1563
02:05:45,840 --> 02:05:46,380
فَاثبُتوا

1564
02:05:46,577 --> 02:05:47,025
Be steadfast

1565
02:05:47,065 --> 02:05:47,603
Number 2)

1566
02:05:48,288 --> 02:05:49,077
وَاذكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثيرًا

1567
02:05:49,117 --> 02:05:49,803
Number 3)

1568
02:05:51,047 --> 02:05:52,222
وَأَطيعُوا اللَّهَ وَرَسولَهُ

1569
02:05:52,293 --> 02:05:52,891
Number 4)

1570
02:05:54,261 --> 02:05:55,075
 وَلا تَنازَعوا

1571
02:05:55,115 --> 02:05:56,121
And Number 5)

1572
02:05:57,392 --> 02:05:58,053
Patience(وَاصبِروا).

1573
02:06:00,212 --> 02:06:03,464
The Ayah(آية) Number 45 and 46 in Al-Anfal(ألأنفال).

1574
02:06:06,285 --> 02:06:10,948
The Mujahideen(مجاهدين) need to be alert and they need to use deception.

1575
02:06:11,729 --> 02:06:12,761
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

1576
02:06:12,801 --> 02:06:13,806
ألحرب خدعة

1577
02:06:13,912 --> 02:06:14,824
War is deception.

1578
02:06:15,126 --> 02:06:16,149
Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

1579
02:06:16,888 --> 02:06:20,346
It is said that when Ali(علي) dueled with Amr Bin Abdwud(عمروبن عبدود),

1580
02:06:20,973 --> 02:06:27,048
Ali(علي) looked over Amr(عمرو)’s shoulder and said: Amr(عمرو) I only came out to fight you, not the two of you.

1581
02:06:28,115 --> 02:06:33,702
Amr(عمرو) looked behind to see who Ali(علي) was talking about and Ali(علي) took advantage of that and struck him.

1582
02:06:35,654 --> 02:06:37,425
 Amr(عمرو) said: You’ve deceived me!

1583
02:06:37,814 --> 02:06:39,721
Ali(علي) said: War is all about deception!

1584
02:06:49,561 --> 02:06:53,718
It is Sunnah(سنت) not to disclose where the army is heading.

1585
02:06:54,678 --> 02:07:00,785
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not disclose his destination in any battle except at Tabook(تبوك)

1586
02:07:00,902 --> 02:07:03,172
because it was against the Romans and was far away.

1587
02:07:03,847 --> 02:07:06,766
He did that in order to have the Muslims prepare accordingly.

1588
02:07:08,796 --> 02:07:13,479
Number 3) The envoy sent to the enemy is a reflection of the army.

1589
02:07:14,486 --> 02:07:20,900
The envoy should be representative of the courage, wisdom, and intelligence of the army and its leadership.

1590
02:07:21,673 --> 02:07:24,839
How many times has an army belittled the enemy

1591
02:07:25,086 --> 02:07:30,778
because of the lack of resolve, foolishness, or weakness of the enemy’s messenger.

1592
02:07:31,648 --> 02:07:40,080
And how many times has an army held the enemy in high esteem due to the dignity, courage, fluency or wisdom of the messenger.

1593
02:07:40,897 --> 02:07:45,177
Therefore the commander needs to make the right choice for this important role.

1594
02:07:46,540 --> 02:07:50,516
The same envoy should not be sent too many times to the same enemy

1595
02:07:51,103 --> 02:07:56,961
in order not to have a personal relationship develop, which could in turn develop into friendship.

1596
02:07:57,574 --> 02:08:02,376
That could eventually lead to a lack of effectiveness in the envoy’s mission.

1597
02:08:02,876 --> 02:08:05,002
It could lead to treason by the envoy.

1598
02:08:05,844 --> 02:08:12,375
So over a long period of time, this Muslim envoy gets closer and closer to the Kuffar(كفار), they host them.

1599
02:08:12,979 --> 02:08:16,271
Check them into five star hotels they feed them the best food.

1600
02:08:16,763 --> 02:08:21,263
And after a while that starts getting to them, and it affects them.

1601
02:08:22,485 --> 02:08:26,723
Don't send them many times because Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) knows how to deceive.

1602
02:08:28,786 --> 02:08:35,836
Number 4) The gatherings of the commander should have readings of the Ahadith(احاديث) of Jihad(جهاد),

1603
02:08:36,492 --> 02:08:42,796
books of Seerah(سيرة), the history of Muslim conquests, the art of war, and stories of the brave.

1604
02:08:43,433 --> 02:08:47,871
That is needed to strengthen the hearts, and relief them from the disease of fear.

1605
02:08:48,925 --> 02:08:53,477
You see, for example in the War of 1967.

1606
02:08:54,135 --> 02:09:05,169
When the Yahood(يهود), bombed Egypt, the generals of the Egyptian army were listening to Um-Kalsoom sings, and they were drinking.

1607
02:09:07,500 --> 02:09:12,337
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says that the army officers in their gatherings,

1608
02:09:12,847 --> 02:09:15,629
should be studying the books of Hadith(حديث) that talk about Jihad(جهاد).

1609
