meaning we have placed restrictions on the interaction that didn't exist in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

1790
02:27:11,879 --> 02:27:14,524
For example, in Masajid(مساجد) the men and women were pray together.

1791
02:27:15,323 --> 02:27:18,204
Women would be behind the men without a curtain or a screen.

1792
02:27:20,180 --> 02:27:22,474
Women would serve men in invitations.

1793
02:27:24,117 --> 02:27:26,511
They would be in hijab(حجاب), and they would serve men.

1794
02:27:27,518 --> 02:27:32,451
And women continued to play a role on the battlefield.

1795
02:27:33,022 --> 02:27:35,030
Even later on in the time of  Al-Khulafa.

1796
02:27:35,546 --> 02:27:40,837
So, you have Nusaiba Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) fighting in the army of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) against Musaylimah Al-Kazab(مسيلمة ألكذاب).

1797
02:27:40,996 --> 02:27:43,115
She actually participated in the fighting itself.

1798
02:27:44,456 --> 02:27:51,522
And they nursed the injured and they served the army.

1799
02:27:52,103 --> 02:27:55,611
So there was a level of interaction there.

1800
02:27:56,246 --> 02:28:02,206
There was a level of interaction there, which is more than what we have today or what we see as acceptable today.

1801
02:28:07,002 --> 02:28:10,223
Do we have time for that? Should I do it tomorrow?

1802
02:28:30,909 --> 02:28:41,172
I did very fast few notes, but I intended on doing more detailed research, I apologize I didn't have the time to.

1803
02:28:41,735 --> 02:28:43,942
But I'll go through what I have now!

1804
02:28:44,553 --> 02:28:51,789
First of all, relating to that issue of in Ghanaim(غنائم) in Darul Harb(دارالحرب),

1805
02:28:52,306 --> 02:28:55,544
we have to talk about the concept of Ghanimah(غنيمه), the concept of  Darul Harb(دارالحرب).

1806
02:28:58,860 --> 02:28:59,618
Al-Ghanimah(غنيمه)

1807
02:29:02,396 --> 02:29:04,444
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

1808
02:29:05,269 --> 02:29:07,180
جُعِل رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

1809
02:29:08,435 --> 02:29:12,370
My Rizq(رزق) comes from under the shade of my spear.

1810
02:29:14,140 --> 02:29:16,570
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has called Ghanimah(غنيمه),

1811
02:29:16,773 --> 02:29:18,030
حلال طيبة

1812
02:29:18,924 --> 02:29:20,205
Halal(حلال) and pure.

1813
02:29:21,829 --> 02:29:27,193
So how come Ghanimah(غنيمه) is considered to be Halal(حلال) and pure?

1814
02:29:31,120 --> 02:29:32,287
Rasool Allah ﷺ says.

1815
02:29:32,367 --> 02:29:34,064
جُعِل رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

1816
02:29:36,629 --> 02:29:39,600
Now why is the Ghanimah(غنيمه) considered to be a high?

1817
02:29:41,671 --> 02:29:44,391
High on the list of Halal(حلال) Rizq(رزق)?

1818
02:29:49,113 --> 02:29:53,034
The reason is, or that's what scholar say,

1819
02:29:55,234 --> 02:30:01,790
is that when somebody is working from nine to five, let's say five days a week,

1820
02:30:02,738 --> 02:30:08,406
that is time taken away from your Da'wah(دعوة), and from your Jihad(جهاد) from serving Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1821
02:30:09,135 --> 02:30:10,960
You're doing it to get Rizq(رزق).

1822
02:30:11,745 --> 02:30:15,269
Everybody says I mean I'm doing it for the sake of Allah to serve the Ummah(امة) and all that.

1823
02:30:15,349 --> 02:30:16,460
But let me ask you this question.

1824
02:30:16,769 --> 02:30:22,095
If, it's really for the sake of all of these lofty reasons.

1825
02:30:22,988 --> 02:30:24,673
Would you still do it if you're not paid?

1826
02:30:26,403 --> 02:30:29,864
So the issue is here is money, you're doing that to make money.

1827
02:30:30,601 --> 02:30:32,205
Let's be straightforward and honest about it.

1828
02:30:32,285 --> 02:30:37,254
You're working because you want that money, you want to lay some food on the table.

1829
02:30:37,913 --> 02:30:41,236
If it was really for the service of religion, that you'd be willing to do it for free,

1830
02:30:41,411 --> 02:30:46,825
which I doubt anybody would be willing to work from nine to five, five days a week for free.

1831
02:30:48,338 --> 02:30:50,250
So the objective is clea, it's for money.

1832
02:30:51,449 --> 02:30:58,735
The Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is devoting his time 24/7 for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1833
02:30:59,514 --> 02:31:02,403
He is not separating any time for seeking Rizq(رزق).

1834
02:31:03,604 --> 02:31:08,635
Ghanimah(غنيمه) comes not as an objective, but as a consequence of Jihad(جهاد).

1835
02:31:10,199 --> 02:31:12,263
A Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

1836
02:31:12,303 --> 02:31:16,391
he is doing it Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) Ghanimah(غنيمه) comes on the side, comes along.

1837
02:31:17,201 --> 02:31:19,985
So the Ghanimah(غنيمه) is a consequence rather than being an objective,

1838
02:31:20,540 --> 02:31:24,621
while when you work, money is the objective, not a consequence.

1839
02:31:25,413 --> 02:31:26,889
You see the difference between the two.

1840
02:31:28,136 --> 02:31:32,513
So, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) had has given his life, his time, his effort for the sake of Allah

1841
02:31:33,037 --> 02:31:35,495
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has rewarded him Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1842
02:31:36,196 --> 02:31:39,936
Therefore, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is better than everybody else.

1843
02:31:40,016 --> 02:31:42,871
And the Rizq(رزق) that he makes is better than any other Rizq(رزق).

1844
02:31:44,881 --> 02:31:54,019
And the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم used to look down at other lines of work, and they will consider that their role is Duat(دُعَاة) to the world.

1845
02:31:54,082 --> 02:32:00,829
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه he heard that some Sahabah(صحابه) started opening up farms in Urdan(أردن).

1846
02:32:01,502 --> 02:32:06,656
They went into Urdan(أردن), and they heard that Yani(يعني) the land over there is very blessed.

1847
02:32:07,462 --> 02:32:09,317
And the returns are great.

1848
02:32:10,152 --> 02:32:15,555
So the Sahabah(صحابه), they started getting themselves busy with farming.

1849
02:32:15,944 --> 02:32:17,460
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sends them letter.

1850
02:32:18,595 --> 02:32:21,189
First of all, he burns all of those farms.

1851
02:32:21,973 --> 02:32:25,909
Just burned them down, and he waited until they were almost going to harvest.

1852
02:32:26,528 --> 02:32:27,441
Alright?

1853
02:32:27,830 --> 02:32:28,713
He burnt it down.

1854
02:32:29,235 --> 02:32:30,601
And then he sent him a letter he said,

1855
02:32:31,474 --> 02:32:38,554
if you are to open farms, and to raise cattle, then you become equal to everybody else.

1856
02:32:39,535 --> 02:32:42,017
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has sent you with Jihad(جهاد) and Da'wah(دعوة).

1857
02:32:44,805 --> 02:32:48,051
In another narration or it might be a different occasion.

1858
02:32:48,537 --> 02:32:58,155
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Who ever raises cattle and starts farming and accepts that as a line of work,

1859
02:32:58,822 --> 02:33:01,157
then I am going to force him to pay Jizya(جِزية).

1860
02:33:03,609 --> 02:33:05,485
Because that is the job of Ahlul Kitab(أهل الكتاب).

1861
02:33:06,397 --> 02:33:09,081
That is the work of Ahlul Kitab(أهل الكتاب), your work is Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1862
02:33:10,189 --> 02:33:14,934
One of the Salaf(سلف), they told him, why don't you get yourself a farm for your kids.

1863
02:33:15,636 --> 02:33:20,957
He says Allah did not send me as a farmer, but he sent me to kill the farmer and take away his crops.

1864
02:33:25,168 --> 02:33:32,676
So you see that the understanding of the Sahabah(صحابه) had, is that our role is to convey the message of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1865
02:33:34,438 --> 02:33:42,047
And let these roles of shepherding and business and farming, let the other people do it.

1866
02:33:42,981 --> 02:33:47,586
We're going to live off Ghanimah(غنيمه) and we're going to guide humanity to Islam.

1867
02:33:48,348 --> 02:33:51,940
People say that Rasool Allah ﷺ was a businessman, he was a businessman before Islam.

1868
02:33:53,713 --> 02:33:57,568
Rasool Allah ﷺ after you started Jihad(جهاد), he didn't really work in any particular profession.

1869
02:33:58,376 --> 02:34:00,009
He wasn't a businessman after that.

1870
02:34:00,502 --> 02:34:04,705
Rasool Allah ﷺ would live from Al-Khums(ألخمس) that he would get from a faye(فيئ).

1871
02:34:06,078 --> 02:34:08,047
And why is a faye(فيئ) called faye(فيئ)?

1872
02:34:09,698 --> 02:34:11,769
Why is faye(فيئ) called faye(فيئ)? Faye(فيئ) means return.

1873
02:34:13,031 --> 02:34:18,347
And the reason why it's called return is because it returns to the lawful owners.

1874
02:34:19,444 --> 02:34:22,428
And that's the second reason why Ghanimah(غنيمه)  made Halal(حلال),

1875
02:34:22,793 --> 02:34:30,678
is because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has created wealth, so that people can establish Salah(صلاة), Zaka'at(زكوة) and islam.

1876
02:34:31,686 --> 02:34:32,321
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

1877
02:34:32,361 --> 02:34:35,818
وَلا تُؤتُوا السُّفَهاءَ أَموالَكُمُ الَّتي جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُم قِيامًا

1878
02:34:36,718 --> 02:34:41,524
Don't give the Sufahaa(سفهاء), the ones with weak minds your wealth,

1879
02:34:42,079 --> 02:34:45,202
because Allah has made wealth Qiyam Lin-Nas(قيام ألناس),

1880
02:34:45,290 --> 02:34:52,060
Qiyam(قيام) means it sustains life, your life depends on money, your existence in this world depends on wealth.

1881
02:34:53,679 --> 02:34:58,787
So Allah has brought down wealth so that the Mo'min(مؤمن) can establish the Ibadah(عبادة) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1882
02:35:01,224 --> 02:35:04,782
So when wealth is in the hands of the Kafir(كافر),

1883
02:35:05,282 --> 02:35:07,853
and what does Kafir(كافر) mean, one who rejects Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

1884
02:35:08,306 --> 02:35:13,096
When the wealth is in the hands of the Kafir(كافر), it is in the hands of somebody who doesn't deserve it.

1885
02:35:14,107 --> 02:35:18,226
So when the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) takes it away from the Kafir(كافر) and puts it in the hands of the Mo'min(مؤمن),

1886
02:35:19,408 --> 02:35:23,024
that is a great blessing because and that makes it Halal(حلال)

1887
02:35:23,064 --> 02:35:29,690
because it is taking the wealth from the hands of the ones who don't deserve it, and putting it in the hands of the ones who deserve it.

1888
02:35:30,725 --> 02:35:32,752
So that's why Ghanimah(غنيمه) is made Halal(حلال).

1889
02:35:33,788 --> 02:35:37,214
It belongs to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and it's going back to the right hands.

1890
02:35:37,653 --> 02:35:41,752
So Al-faye(الفيئ) is wealth, coming back to its rightful owners.

1891
02:35:43,224 --> 02:35:45,529
So that's the concept of the Ghanimah(غنيمه) itself.

1892
02:35:45,806 --> 02:35:49,393
Because sometimes people have this doubts in their mind.

1893
02:35:50,544 --> 02:35:54,480
How can Sahabah(صحابه) live off the money of some other people, they work for their lives,

1894
02:35:54,536 --> 02:35:55,760
and then Sahabah(صحابه) come and take it.

1895
02:35:56,522 --> 02:36:01,343
The issue is here that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are appointed by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to spread the religion.

1896
02:36:01,589 --> 02:36:04,837
The wealth belongs to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wants to give them this wealth

1897
02:36:04,885 --> 02:36:08,194
so that they can carry on Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) and giving Da'wah(دعوة).

1898
02:36:08,940 --> 02:36:11,905
And these people whom the Sahabah(صحابه) brought Islam, need to pay for that.

1899
02:36:12,464 --> 02:36:14,710
So that's the concept of Ghanimah(غنيمه) itself so that you understand

1900
02:36:14,789 --> 02:36:20,686
how come Ghanimah(غنيمه) is such a great blessing of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, and how come is to the purest form of Rizq(رزق).

1901
02:36:21,483 --> 02:36:23,332
When Abdul Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) passed away,

1902
02:36:23,823 --> 02:36:31,397
he in his will, he said that he should give part of my wealth to everybody who attended the Battle of badr(بدر).

1903
02:36:31,722 --> 02:36:39,423
So they brought up Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) some money, and they said, this is from Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن).

1904
02:36:39,629 --> 02:36:43,893
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), at the time was the Khalifah(خليفه), and he was a businessman, he was wealthy,

1905
02:36:44,119 --> 02:36:46,409
 but he accepted the money of Abdul Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) because he said:

1906
02:36:46,821 --> 02:36:49,921
It is 100% Halal(حلال), it's coming from Ghanaem(غنائم).

1907
02:36:50,001 --> 02:36:51,854
It's coming from Ghanaem(غنائم) that he invests.

1908
02:36:55,381 --> 02:36:58,064
The second issue, taking Ghanimah(غنيمه) from Dar Ul-Harb(دارالحرب)

1909
02:36:58,104 --> 02:37:02,975
and whether these areas would be classified as Dar Ul-Harb(دارالحرب).

1910
02:37:03,532 --> 02:37:11,205
I think that, for us, the issue should be beyond having second thoughts on whether this is Dar Ul-Harb(دارالحرب) or not.

1911
02:37:11,850 --> 02:37:15,363
And I don't think it's even time for us to discuss the evidences for that.

1912
02:37:15,915 --> 02:37:20,499
It's an issue that is beyond discussion, it shouldn't be clear, and it should be common knowledge,

1913
02:37:20,899 --> 02:37:26,370
and the straw that broke the camel's back is Iraq, but that's just a straw.

1914
02:37:29,092 --> 02:37:40,814
So from a Fiqh(فقه) point of view, there's no issue here was the legality of taking Ghanaem(غنائم),

1915
02:37:42,624 --> 02:37:44,586
from strictly Shariah(شريعة) point of view.

1916
02:37:45,227 --> 02:37:52,176
However, there are some statement needs to be studied,

1917
02:37:52,892 --> 02:37:59,791
from Fiqh Al-Waqiah(فقه الواقع) point of view and a strategic point of view, you have two concerns.

1918
02:38:00,284 --> 02:38:03,157
Number one, money and Uraz(عراض).

1919
02:38:03,356 --> 02:38:05,679
ألمال والعرض ودم

1920
02:38:06,901 --> 02:38:12,108
 these three issues, blood wealth, and Urraz(عرض), women.

1921
02:38:14,769 --> 02:38:20,506
Because there's room for corruption in these three areas.

1922
02:38:21,745 --> 02:38:28,862
Islam has placed restrictions, so that these three areas are not handled on an individual basis,

1923
02:38:29,304 --> 02:38:31,244
but they are handled on a collective basis.

1924
02:38:32,558 --> 02:38:35,712
So only a Jama'ah(جماعة) can take a decision in these areas.

1925
02:38:36,756 --> 02:38:41,127
When it comes to the demaa(دماء), the blood of people, when it comes to the wealth of people,

1926
02:38:41,504 --> 02:38:46,515
and when it comes to Al-Uraz(ألعراض), woman, it must be done in a collective way

1927
02:38:46,887 --> 02:38:49,744
through the permission of an Ameer(أمير) and Shurah(شورى).

1928
02:38:50,735 --> 02:38:53,560
It is not an issue that is taken into individual hands.

1929
02:38:54,402 --> 02:38:59,370
And this is very clear from Shariah(شريعة) point of view,

1930
02:39:00,470 --> 02:39:02,994
the role that is given to the Ameer(أمير) in applying Hadd(حدّ).

1931
02:39:04,050 --> 02:39:05,634
These issues were given to Amara(أمارة),

1932
02:39:05,682 --> 02:39:05,881
why?

1933
02:39:05,911 --> 02:39:11,044
Because there's room for a lot of corruption in these areas.

1934
02:39:11,578 --> 02:39:15,727
These areas are open for people to take matters into their own hands,

1935
02:39:16,227 --> 02:39:19,344
there will be Fasad Fil Ardh(فساد فى الأرض), there will be corruption on land.

1936
02:39:20,878 --> 02:39:22,800
And it will lead to a chaotic stage.

1937
02:39:24,179 --> 02:39:31,477
So when it comes to these issues, the decision is made through a Jama'ah(جماعة) and through an Ameer(أمير).

1938
02:39:34,534 --> 02:39:39,983
The second concern, the reputation of Muslims is a valid concern.

1939
02:39:41,427 --> 02:39:43,833
The reputation of Muslims is a valid concern.

1940
02:39:46,730 --> 02:39:53,218
It is not good for the Muslims to have a reputation of being burglars of being rapists

1941
02:39:54,210 --> 02:39:58,670
and Rasool Allah ﷺ did take such matters in consideration.

1942
02:39:59,146 --> 02:40:02,411
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was told by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

1943
02:40:02,491 --> 02:40:07,546
to kill Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَيئ), who was the head of Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) and he deserved to be executed.

1944
02:40:08,856 --> 02:40:10,149
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

1945
02:40:10,340 --> 02:40:10,634
He said:

1946
02:40:10,674 --> 02:40:14,065
لا أريد ان يقول لي حد بالناس من محمدٍ يقتل اصحابه

1947
02:40:14,484 --> 02:40:18,030
I don't want people to go around saying that Muhammad(محمد) is killing his followers.

1948
02:40:18,857 --> 02:40:21,484
So he didn't disagree with the fact that he deserves to die.

1949
02:40:22,118 --> 02:40:25,785
But he said that it's not good for the reputation of Muslims.

1950
02:40:27,023 --> 02:40:31,291
That's the only reason I'm not going to kill him because I don't want people to say that Muhammad(محمد) is killing his followers.

1951
02:40:31,994 --> 02:40:35,790
That will turn people away from Islam, they're gonna say we're not going to follow a man who will end up killing us.

1952
02:40:36,637 --> 02:40:41,785
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ withheld that decision and did not execute Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَيئ)

1953
02:40:41,825 --> 02:40:47,766
who has called has caused so much Fitnah(فِتْنَه), and so much disunity, and so much Fasad(فساد) in the Muslim community.

1954
02:40:48,237 --> 02:40:50,769
Rasool Allah ﷺ had patience in that regard.

1955
02:40:51,285 --> 02:40:52,624
So the reputation is important.

1956
02:40:52,997 --> 02:40:57,410
If the Muslims still have a good reputation in such areas, they should be careful.

1957
02:40:57,822 --> 02:41:02,261
If the reputation is already tarnished and gone, then that is not a concern anymore.

1958
02:41:02,918 --> 02:41:09,801
The third concern regarding, this issue is, in my view, and I've heard

1959
02:41:09,952 --> 02:41:13,852
Yani(يعني) two other opinions that I heard are contrary to this.

1960
02:41:16,931 --> 02:41:21,441
All of such money needs to be dealt with as faye(فيئ) and not Ghanimah(غنيمه),

1961
02:41:22,372 --> 02:41:26,840
it should be dealt as if it is Faye(فيئ) and not Ghanimah(غنيمه).

1962
02:41:26,951 --> 02:41:33,763
Therefore, none of it, goes to the individual, the entire amount goes to the Jama'at(جماعة).

1963
02:41:35,076 --> 02:41:41,078
And that's also a safety valve to make sure that people are not going to start doing things for their own personal gain and benefit.

1964
02:41:41,118 --> 02:41:48,570
And that is Fasad(فساد), and also from Fiqh(فقه) point of view, it looks like faye(فيئ), there is no fighting involved.

1965
02:41:48,642 --> 02:41:49,673
So how can it be Ghanimah(غنيمه)?

1966
02:41:49,713 --> 02:41:54,455
